[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3","title":"Cerebras CS-3 晶圓尺度叢集","titleEn":"Cerebras CS-3 wafer-scale cluster","category":"computing","subcategory":"ai-wafer","subcategoryTitle":"晶圓尺度計算","subcategoryTitleEn":"Wafer-scale compute","learningTrack":"ai","learningSubdiscipline":"ai-wafer","learningTags":["ai","ai-wafer","cerebras-cs3"],"kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"curriculumVersion":11,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":420,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"stages":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-stage1","order":1,"title":"系統邊界與基本原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and principles","description":"在Cerebras CS-3 晶圓尺度叢集案例中比較WSE本地core與SRAM與MemoryX參數流，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate wse local cores and sram and memoryx parameter streaming within the Cerebras CS-3 wafer-scale cluster case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"title":"晶圓網格與局部記憶：架構分析","titleEn":"Wafer meshes and local memory: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"針對WSE本地core與SRAM提出可反駁的晶圓網格與局部記憶模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable wafer meshes and local memory model and evidence record for wse local cores and sram.","instruction":"在「Cerebras CS-3 晶圓尺度叢集」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識WSE本地core與SRAM。晶圓尺度將多核心與本地SRAM相連；避開部分離片搬運但仍有通信和容量限制。 建立晶圓網格與局部記憶的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是本地 SRAM、權重串流與晶圓尺度通信。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。比較鄰近交換與跨片搬運的假想bytes。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify wse local cores and sram in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Cerebras CS-3 wafer-scale cluster. Wafer-scale cores connect local SRAM; some off-chip traffic is avoided, with remaining capacity/communication limits. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of wafer meshes and local memory, focusing on local sram, weight streaming and wafer-scale communication. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Compare assumed neighbor exchange and off-chip bytes. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"比較鄰近交換與跨片搬運的假想bytes。","observationEn":"Compare assumed neighbor exchange and off-chip bytes.","failure":"常見誤判：沒有傳統cache就表示記憶體無限。","failureEn":"Common misconception: No conventional cache means unlimited memory.","check":"提交WSE本地core與SRAM的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for wse local cores and sram.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-01-k1","title":"晶圓網格與局部記憶","titleEn":"Wafer meshes and local memory","text":"晶圓尺度將多核心與本地SRAM相連；避開部分離片搬運但仍有通信和容量限制。 本課架構對應：WSE本地core與SRAM","textEn":"Wafer-scale cores connect local SRAM; some off-chip traffic is avoided, with remaining capacity/communication limits. Course architecture correspondence: WSE local cores and SRAM","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-01-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較鄰近交換與跨片搬運的假想bytes。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；沒有傳統cache就表示記憶體無限。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed neighbor exchange and off-chip bytes. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: No conventional cache means unlimited memory.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-01-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設算術強度 I=6 FLOP/byte、頻寬 B=0.9 TB/s、計算峯值 42 TFLOP/s，理想 roofline=min(42,I×B)=5.4 TFLOP/s。皆非產品規格，未含同步、精度轉換或工作形狀損失。","textEn":"Assume I=6 FLOP/byte, B=0.9 TB/s and compute peak 42 TFLOP/s: ideal roofline min(42,I×B)=5.4 TFLOP/s. These are not product specifications; synchronization, precision conversion and shape inefficiency are omitted.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就WSE本地core與SRAM的「晶圓網格與局部記憶」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for wafer meshes and local memory in wse local cores and sram?","options":["晶圓尺度將多核心與本地SRAM相連；避開部分離片搬運但仍有通信和容量限制。","沒有傳統cache就表示記憶體無限。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Wafer-scale cores connect local SRAM; some off-chip traffic is avoided, with remaining capacity/communication limits.","No conventional cache means unlimited memory.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶圓尺度將多核心與本地SRAM相連；避開部分離片搬運但仍有通信和容量限制。 比較鄰近交換與跨片搬運的假想bytes。","explanationEn":"Wafer-scale cores connect local SRAM; some off-chip traffic is avoided, with remaining capacity/communication limits. Compare assumed neighbor exchange and off-chip bytes."}},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"title":"晶圓網格與局部記憶：證據驗證","titleEn":"Wafer meshes and local memory: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-01"],"objective":"針對WSE本地core與SRAM提出可反駁的晶圓網格與局部記憶模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable wafer meshes and local memory model and evidence record for wse local cores and sram.","instruction":"沿用前一步「晶圓網格與局部記憶」模型，檢查WSE本地core與SRAM的兩個假想案例。比較鄰近交換與跨片搬運的假想bytes。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分晶圓尺度將多核心與本地SRAM相連；避開部分離片搬運但仍有通信和容量限制。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous wafer meshes and local memory model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving wse local cores and sram. Compare assumed neighbor exchange and off-chip bytes. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Wafer-scale cores connect local SRAM; some off-chip traffic is avoided, with remaining capacity/communication limits.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"比較鄰近交換與跨片搬運的假想bytes。","observationEn":"Compare assumed neighbor exchange and off-chip bytes.","failure":"常見誤判：沒有傳統cache就表示記憶體無限。","failureEn":"Common misconception: No conventional cache means unlimited memory.","check":"提交WSE本地core與SRAM的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for wse local cores and sram.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-02-k1","title":"晶圓網格與局部記憶","titleEn":"Wafer meshes and local memory","text":"晶圓尺度將多核心與本地SRAM相連；避開部分離片搬運但仍有通信和容量限制。 本課架構對應：WSE本地core與SRAM","textEn":"Wafer-scale cores connect local SRAM; some off-chip traffic is avoided, with remaining capacity/communication limits. Course architecture correspondence: WSE local cores and SRAM","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-02-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較鄰近交換與跨片搬運的假想bytes。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；沒有傳統cache就表示記憶體無限。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed neighbor exchange and off-chip bytes. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: No conventional cache means unlimited memory.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-02-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設算術強度 I=6 FLOP/byte、頻寬 B=0.9 TB/s、計算峯值 42 TFLOP/s，理想 roofline=min(42,I×B)=5.4 TFLOP/s。皆非產品規格，未含同步、精度轉換或工作形狀損失。","textEn":"Assume I=6 FLOP/byte, B=0.9 TB/s and compute peak 42 TFLOP/s: ideal roofline min(42,I×B)=5.4 TFLOP/s. These are not product specifications; synchronization, precision conversion and shape inefficiency are omitted.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就WSE本地core與SRAM的「晶圓網格與局部記憶」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for wafer meshes and local memory in wse local cores and sram?","options":["沒有傳統cache就表示記憶體無限。","比較鄰近交換與跨片搬運的假想bytes。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["No conventional cache means unlimited memory.","Compare assumed neighbor exchange and off-chip bytes.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶圓尺度將多核心與本地SRAM相連；避開部分離片搬運但仍有通信和容量限制。 比較鄰近交換與跨片搬運的假想bytes。","explanationEn":"Wafer-scale cores connect local SRAM; some off-chip traffic is avoided, with remaining capacity/communication limits. Compare assumed neighbor exchange and off-chip bytes."}},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"title":"權重串流與分離：架構分析","titleEn":"Weight streaming and disaggregation: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-02"],"objective":"針對MemoryX參數流提出可反駁的權重串流與分離模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable weight streaming and disaggregation model and evidence record for memoryx parameter streaming.","instruction":"在「Cerebras CS-3 晶圓尺度叢集」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識MemoryX參數流。參數可存於獨立記憶系統並串流到計算；通信帶寬與更新一致性是關鍵邊界。 建立權重串流與分離的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是本地 SRAM、權重串流與晶圓尺度通信。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。畫前傳、反傳及參數更新的方向。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify memoryx parameter streaming in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Cerebras CS-3 wafer-scale cluster. Separate memory can stream weights to compute; bandwidth and update consistency remain key. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of weight streaming and disaggregation, focusing on local sram, weight streaming and wafer-scale communication. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Draw forward, backward and update directions. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"畫前傳、反傳及參數更新的方向。","observationEn":"Draw forward, backward and update directions.","failure":"常見誤判：參數與計算分離就完全不需要通信。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Disaggregating parameters removes communication.","check":"提交MemoryX參數流的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for memoryx parameter streaming.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-03-k1","title":"權重串流與分離","titleEn":"Weight streaming and disaggregation","text":"參數可存於獨立記憶系統並串流到計算；通信帶寬與更新一致性是關鍵邊界。 本課架構對應：MemoryX參數流","textEn":"Separate memory can stream weights to compute; bandwidth and update consistency remain key. Course architecture correspondence: MemoryX parameter streaming","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-03-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫前傳、反傳及參數更新的方向。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；參數與計算分離就完全不需要通信。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw forward, backward and update directions. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Disaggregating parameters removes communication.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就MemoryX參數流的「權重串流與分離」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for weight streaming and disaggregation in memoryx parameter streaming?","options":["參數與計算分離就完全不需要通信。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","參數可存於獨立記憶系統並串流到計算；通信帶寬與更新一致性是關鍵邊界。"],"optionsEn":["Disaggregating parameters removes communication.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Separate memory can stream weights to compute; bandwidth and update consistency remain key."],"answer":2,"explanation":"參數可存於獨立記憶系統並串流到計算；通信帶寬與更新一致性是關鍵邊界。 畫前傳、反傳及參數更新的方向。","explanationEn":"Separate memory can stream weights to compute; bandwidth and update consistency remain key. Draw forward, backward and update directions."}},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"title":"權重串流與分離：證據驗證","titleEn":"Weight streaming and disaggregation: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-03"],"objective":"針對MemoryX參數流提出可反駁的權重串流與分離模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable weight streaming and disaggregation model and evidence record for memoryx parameter streaming.","instruction":"沿用前一步「權重串流與分離」模型，檢查MemoryX參數流的兩個假想案例。畫前傳、反傳及參數更新的方向。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分參數可存於獨立記憶系統並串流到計算；通信帶寬與更新一致性是關鍵邊界。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous weight streaming and disaggregation model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving memoryx parameter streaming. Draw forward, backward and update directions. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Separate memory can stream weights to compute; bandwidth and update consistency remain key.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"畫前傳、反傳及參數更新的方向。","observationEn":"Draw forward, backward and update directions.","failure":"常見誤判：參數與計算分離就完全不需要通信。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Disaggregating parameters removes communication.","check":"提交MemoryX參數流的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for memoryx parameter streaming.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-04-k1","title":"權重串流與分離","titleEn":"Weight streaming and disaggregation","text":"參數可存於獨立記憶系統並串流到計算；通信帶寬與更新一致性是關鍵邊界。 本課架構對應：MemoryX參數流","textEn":"Separate memory can stream weights to compute; bandwidth and update consistency remain key. Course architecture correspondence: MemoryX parameter streaming","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-04-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫前傳、反傳及參數更新的方向。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；參數與計算分離就完全不需要通信。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw forward, backward and update directions. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Disaggregating parameters removes communication.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就MemoryX參數流的「權重串流與分離」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for weight streaming and disaggregation in memoryx parameter streaming?","options":["畫前傳、反傳及參數更新的方向。","參數與計算分離就完全不需要通信。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Draw forward, backward and update directions.","Disaggregating parameters removes communication.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"參數可存於獨立記憶系統並串流到計算；通信帶寬與更新一致性是關鍵邊界。 畫前傳、反傳及參數更新的方向。","explanationEn":"Separate memory can stream weights to compute; bandwidth and update consistency remain key. Draw forward, backward and update directions."}}]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-stage2","order":2,"title":"功能架構與量化模型","titleEn":"Functional architecture and quantitative models","description":"在Cerebras CS-3 晶圓尺度叢集案例中比較稀疏計算mapping與晶圓冗餘繞路，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate sparse compute mapping and wafer redundancy and rerouting within the Cerebras CS-3 wafer-scale cluster case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"title":"稀疏映射與負載：架構分析","titleEn":"Sparse mapping and load: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-04"],"objective":"針對稀疏計算mapping提出可反駁的稀疏映射與負載模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable sparse mapping and load model and evidence record for sparse compute mapping.","instruction":"在「Cerebras CS-3 晶圓尺度叢集」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識稀疏計算mapping。稀疏數據可減少算術，但不均勻分配可能形成局部瓶頸。 建立稀疏映射與負載的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是本地 SRAM、權重串流與晶圓尺度通信。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。比較均勻與聚集稀疏分佈的最慢核心負載。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify sparse compute mapping in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Cerebras CS-3 wafer-scale cluster. Sparsity reduces arithmetic while uneven mapping can create local bottlenecks. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of sparse mapping and load, focusing on local sram, weight streaming and wafer-scale communication. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Compare slowest-core load for uniform/clustered sparsity. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"比較均勻與聚集稀疏分佈的最慢核心負載。","observationEn":"Compare slowest-core load for uniform/clustered sparsity.","failure":"常見誤判：零元素比例相同表示執行速度相同。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal zero fractions imply equal runtime.","check":"提交稀疏計算mapping的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for sparse compute mapping.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-05-k1","title":"稀疏映射與負載","titleEn":"Sparse mapping and load","text":"稀疏數據可減少算術，但不均勻分配可能形成局部瓶頸。 本課架構對應：稀疏計算mapping","textEn":"Sparsity reduces arithmetic while uneven mapping can create local bottlenecks. Course architecture correspondence: Sparse compute mapping","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-05-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較均勻與聚集稀疏分佈的最慢核心負載。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；零元素比例相同表示執行速度相同。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare slowest-core load for uniform/clustered sparsity. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Equal zero fractions imply equal runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就稀疏計算mapping的「稀疏映射與負載」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for sparse mapping and load in sparse compute mapping?","options":["零元素比例相同表示執行速度相同。","稀疏數據可減少算術，但不均勻分配可能形成局部瓶頸。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Equal zero fractions imply equal runtime.","Sparsity reduces arithmetic while uneven mapping can create local bottlenecks.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"稀疏數據可減少算術，但不均勻分配可能形成局部瓶頸。 比較均勻與聚集稀疏分佈的最慢核心負載。","explanationEn":"Sparsity reduces arithmetic while uneven mapping can create local bottlenecks. Compare slowest-core load for uniform/clustered sparsity."}},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"title":"稀疏映射與負載：證據驗證","titleEn":"Sparse mapping and load: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-05"],"objective":"針對稀疏計算mapping提出可反駁的稀疏映射與負載模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable sparse mapping and load model and evidence record for sparse compute mapping.","instruction":"沿用前一步「稀疏映射與負載」模型，檢查稀疏計算mapping的兩個假想案例。比較均勻與聚集稀疏分佈的最慢核心負載。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分稀疏數據可減少算術，但不均勻分配可能形成局部瓶頸。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous sparse mapping and load model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving sparse compute mapping. Compare slowest-core load for uniform/clustered sparsity. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Sparsity reduces arithmetic while uneven mapping can create local bottlenecks.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"比較均勻與聚集稀疏分佈的最慢核心負載。","observationEn":"Compare slowest-core load for uniform/clustered sparsity.","failure":"常見誤判：零元素比例相同表示執行速度相同。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal zero fractions imply equal runtime.","check":"提交稀疏計算mapping的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for sparse compute mapping.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-06-k1","title":"稀疏映射與負載","titleEn":"Sparse mapping and load","text":"稀疏數據可減少算術，但不均勻分配可能形成局部瓶頸。 本課架構對應：稀疏計算mapping","textEn":"Sparsity reduces arithmetic while uneven mapping can create local bottlenecks. Course architecture correspondence: Sparse compute mapping","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-06-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較均勻與聚集稀疏分佈的最慢核心負載。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；零元素比例相同表示執行速度相同。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare slowest-core load for uniform/clustered sparsity. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Equal zero fractions imply equal runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就稀疏計算mapping的「稀疏映射與負載」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for sparse mapping and load in sparse compute mapping?","options":["零元素比例相同表示執行速度相同。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","比較均勻與聚集稀疏分佈的最慢核心負載。"],"optionsEn":["Equal zero fractions imply equal runtime.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Compare slowest-core load for uniform/clustered sparsity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"稀疏數據可減少算術，但不均勻分配可能形成局部瓶頸。 比較均勻與聚集稀疏分佈的最慢核心負載。","explanationEn":"Sparsity reduces arithmetic while uneven mapping can create local bottlenecks. Compare slowest-core load for uniform/clustered sparsity."}},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"title":"晶圓容錯與良率：架構分析","titleEn":"Wafer redundancy and yield: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-06"],"objective":"針對晶圓冗餘繞路提出可反駁的晶圓容錯與良率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable wafer redundancy and yield model and evidence record for wafer redundancy and rerouting.","instruction":"在「Cerebras CS-3 晶圓尺度叢集」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識晶圓冗餘繞路。大面積設計需面對缺陷；冗餘與繞路形成可用資源而非完美晶圓。 建立晶圓容錯與良率的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是本地 SRAM、權重串流與晶圓尺度通信。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。在假想缺陷圖檢查重映射後的連通及容量。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify wafer redundancy and rerouting in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Cerebras CS-3 wafer-scale cluster. Large-area designs face defects; redundancy/rerouting create usable resources, not flawless wafers. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of wafer redundancy and yield, focusing on local sram, weight streaming and wafer-scale communication. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Check connectivity/capacity after remapping an assumed defect map. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"在假想缺陷圖檢查重映射後的連通及容量。","observationEn":"Check connectivity/capacity after remapping an assumed defect map.","failure":"常見誤判：可用晶圓即表示每個物理核心都無缺陷。","failureEn":"Common misconception: A usable wafer means every physical core is defect-free.","check":"提交晶圓冗餘繞路的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for wafer redundancy and rerouting.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-07-k1","title":"晶圓容錯與良率","titleEn":"Wafer redundancy and yield","text":"大面積設計需面對缺陷；冗餘與繞路形成可用資源而非完美晶圓。 本課架構對應：晶圓冗餘繞路","textEn":"Large-area designs face defects; redundancy/rerouting create usable resources, not flawless wafers. Course architecture correspondence: Wafer redundancy and rerouting","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-07-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在假想缺陷圖檢查重映射後的連通及容量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；可用晶圓即表示每個物理核心都無缺陷。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check connectivity/capacity after remapping an assumed defect map. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: A usable wafer means every physical core is defect-free.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就晶圓冗餘繞路的「晶圓容錯與良率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for wafer redundancy and yield in wafer redundancy and rerouting?","options":["大面積設計需面對缺陷；冗餘與繞路形成可用資源而非完美晶圓。","可用晶圓即表示每個物理核心都無缺陷。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Large-area designs face defects; redundancy/rerouting create usable resources, not flawless wafers.","A usable wafer means every physical core is defect-free.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"大面積設計需面對缺陷；冗餘與繞路形成可用資源而非完美晶圓。 在假想缺陷圖檢查重映射後的連通及容量。","explanationEn":"Large-area designs face defects; redundancy/rerouting create usable resources, not flawless wafers. Check connectivity/capacity after remapping an assumed defect map."}},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"title":"晶圓容錯與良率：證據驗證","titleEn":"Wafer redundancy and yield: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-07"],"objective":"針對晶圓冗餘繞路提出可反駁的晶圓容錯與良率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable wafer redundancy and yield model and evidence record for wafer redundancy and rerouting.","instruction":"沿用前一步「晶圓容錯與良率」模型，檢查晶圓冗餘繞路的兩個假想案例。在假想缺陷圖檢查重映射後的連通及容量。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分大面積設計需面對缺陷；冗餘與繞路形成可用資源而非完美晶圓。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous wafer redundancy and yield model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving wafer redundancy and rerouting. Check connectivity/capacity after remapping an assumed defect map. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Large-area designs face defects; redundancy/rerouting create usable resources, not flawless wafers.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"在假想缺陷圖檢查重映射後的連通及容量。","observationEn":"Check connectivity/capacity after remapping an assumed defect map.","failure":"常見誤判：可用晶圓即表示每個物理核心都無缺陷。","failureEn":"Common misconception: A usable wafer means every physical core is defect-free.","check":"提交晶圓冗餘繞路的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for wafer redundancy and rerouting.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-08-k1","title":"晶圓容錯與良率","titleEn":"Wafer redundancy and yield","text":"大面積設計需面對缺陷；冗餘與繞路形成可用資源而非完美晶圓。 本課架構對應：晶圓冗餘繞路","textEn":"Large-area designs face defects; redundancy/rerouting create usable resources, not flawless wafers. Course architecture correspondence: Wafer redundancy and rerouting","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-08-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在假想缺陷圖檢查重映射後的連通及容量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；可用晶圓即表示每個物理核心都無缺陷。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check connectivity/capacity after remapping an assumed defect map. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: A usable wafer means every physical core is defect-free.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就晶圓冗餘繞路的「晶圓容錯與良率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for wafer redundancy and yield in wafer redundancy and rerouting?","options":["可用晶圓即表示每個物理核心都無缺陷。","在假想缺陷圖檢查重映射後的連通及容量。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["A usable wafer means every physical core is defect-free.","Check connectivity/capacity after remapping an assumed defect map.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"大面積設計需面對缺陷；冗餘與繞路形成可用資源而非完美晶圓。 在假想缺陷圖檢查重映射後的連通及容量。","explanationEn":"Large-area designs face defects; redundancy/rerouting create usable resources, not flawless wafers. Check connectivity/capacity after remapping an assumed defect map."}}]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-stage3","order":3,"title":"獨立驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Independent validation and engineering handoff","description":"在Cerebras CS-3 晶圓尺度叢集案例中比較多CS系統梯度與晶圓與設施散熱，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate multi-cs system gradients and wafer/facility cooling within the Cerebras CS-3 wafer-scale cluster case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"title":"叢集擴充與參數同步：架構分析","titleEn":"Cluster scaling and synchronization: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-08"],"objective":"針對多CS系統梯度提出可反駁的叢集擴充與參數同步模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable cluster scaling and synchronization model and evidence record for multi-cs system gradients.","instruction":"在「Cerebras CS-3 晶圓尺度叢集」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識多CS系統梯度。多個系統共享參數與同步梯度，擴充效率還取決於網絡和批次。 建立叢集擴充與參數同步的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是本地 SRAM、權重串流與晶圓尺度通信。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。固定全局批次比較單系統與多系統效率。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify multi-cs system gradients in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Cerebras CS-3 wafer-scale cluster. Systems share parameters/synchronize gradients; network and batches still limit scaling. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of cluster scaling and synchronization, focusing on local sram, weight streaming and wafer-scale communication. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Compare one/many-system efficiency at fixed global batch. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"固定全局批次比較單系統與多系統效率。","observationEn":"Compare one/many-system efficiency at fixed global batch.","failure":"常見誤判：增加系統必然線性加速所有模型。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Adding systems linearly speeds every model.","check":"提交多CS系統梯度的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for multi-cs system gradients.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-09-k1","title":"叢集擴充與參數同步","titleEn":"Cluster scaling and synchronization","text":"多個系統共享參數與同步梯度，擴充效率還取決於網絡和批次。 本課架構對應：多CS系統梯度","textEn":"Systems share parameters/synchronize gradients; network and batches still limit scaling. Course architecture correspondence: Multi-CS system gradients","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-09-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"固定全局批次比較單系統與多系統效率。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；增加系統必然線性加速所有模型。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare one/many-system efficiency at fixed global batch. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Adding systems linearly speeds every model.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就多CS系統梯度的「叢集擴充與參數同步」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for cluster scaling and synchronization in multi-cs system gradients?","options":["增加系統必然線性加速所有模型。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","多個系統共享參數與同步梯度，擴充效率還取決於網絡和批次。"],"optionsEn":["Adding systems linearly speeds every model.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Systems share parameters/synchronize gradients; network and batches still limit scaling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多個系統共享參數與同步梯度，擴充效率還取決於網絡和批次。 固定全局批次比較單系統與多系統效率。","explanationEn":"Systems share parameters/synchronize gradients; network and batches still limit scaling. Compare one/many-system efficiency at fixed global batch."}},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"title":"叢集擴充與參數同步：證據驗證","titleEn":"Cluster scaling and synchronization: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-09"],"objective":"針對多CS系統梯度提出可反駁的叢集擴充與參數同步模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable cluster scaling and synchronization model and evidence record for multi-cs system gradients.","instruction":"沿用前一步「叢集擴充與參數同步」模型，檢查多CS系統梯度的兩個假想案例。固定全局批次比較單系統與多系統效率。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分多個系統共享參數與同步梯度，擴充效率還取決於網絡和批次。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous cluster scaling and synchronization model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving multi-cs system gradients. Compare one/many-system efficiency at fixed global batch. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Systems share parameters/synchronize gradients; network and batches still limit scaling.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"固定全局批次比較單系統與多系統效率。","observationEn":"Compare one/many-system efficiency at fixed global batch.","failure":"常見誤判：增加系統必然線性加速所有模型。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Adding systems linearly speeds every model.","check":"提交多CS系統梯度的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for multi-cs system gradients.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-10-k1","title":"叢集擴充與參數同步","titleEn":"Cluster scaling and synchronization","text":"多個系統共享參數與同步梯度，擴充效率還取決於網絡和批次。 本課架構對應：多CS系統梯度","textEn":"Systems share parameters/synchronize gradients; network and batches still limit scaling. Course architecture correspondence: Multi-CS system gradients","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-10-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"固定全局批次比較單系統與多系統效率。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；增加系統必然線性加速所有模型。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare one/many-system efficiency at fixed global batch. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Adding systems linearly speeds every model.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就多CS系統梯度的「叢集擴充與參數同步」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for cluster scaling and synchronization in multi-cs system gradients?","options":["固定全局批次比較單系統與多系統效率。","增加系統必然線性加速所有模型。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Compare one/many-system efficiency at fixed global batch.","Adding systems linearly speeds every model.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多個系統共享參數與同步梯度，擴充效率還取決於網絡和批次。 固定全局批次比較單系統與多系統效率。","explanationEn":"Systems share parameters/synchronize gradients; network and batches still limit scaling. Compare one/many-system efficiency at fixed global batch."}},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"title":"冷卻與工作能量：架構分析","titleEn":"Cooling and job energy: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-10"],"objective":"針對晶圓與設施散熱提出可反駁的冷卻與工作能量模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable cooling and job energy model and evidence record for wafer/facility cooling.","instruction":"在「Cerebras CS-3 晶圓尺度叢集」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識晶圓與設施散熱。芯片、供電與冷卻形成不同效率層；裸芯片性能不是完整系統能效。 建立冷卻與工作能量的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是本地 SRAM、權重串流與晶圓尺度通信。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。把計算、通信與設施能量分別列表。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify wafer/facility cooling in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Cerebras CS-3 wafer-scale cluster. Chip, power delivery and cooling have separate efficiencies; chip performance is not system energy efficiency. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of cooling and job energy, focusing on local sram, weight streaming and wafer-scale communication. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. List compute, communication and facility energy separately. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"把計算、通信與設施能量分別列表。","observationEn":"List compute, communication and facility energy separately.","failure":"常見誤判：芯片指標即可取代設施能耗量測。","failureEn":"Common misconception: A chip metric replaces facility energy measurement.","check":"提交晶圓與設施散熱的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for wafer/facility cooling.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-11-k1","title":"冷卻與工作能量","titleEn":"Cooling and job energy","text":"芯片、供電與冷卻形成不同效率層；裸芯片性能不是完整系統能效。 本課架構對應：晶圓與設施散熱","textEn":"Chip, power delivery and cooling have separate efficiencies; chip performance is not system energy efficiency. Course architecture correspondence: Wafer/facility cooling","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-11-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"把計算、通信與設施能量分別列表。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；芯片指標即可取代設施能耗量測。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"List compute, communication and facility energy separately. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: A chip metric replaces facility energy measurement.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-11-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設算術強度 I=6 FLOP/byte、頻寬 B=0.9 TB/s、計算峯值 42 TFLOP/s，理想 roofline=min(42,I×B)=5.4 TFLOP/s。皆非產品規格，未含同步、精度轉換或工作形狀損失。","textEn":"Assume I=6 FLOP/byte, B=0.9 TB/s and compute peak 42 TFLOP/s: ideal roofline min(42,I×B)=5.4 TFLOP/s. These are not product specifications; synchronization, precision conversion and shape inefficiency are omitted.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就晶圓與設施散熱的「冷卻與工作能量」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for cooling and job energy in wafer/facility cooling?","options":["芯片指標即可取代設施能耗量測。","芯片、供電與冷卻形成不同效率層；裸芯片性能不是完整系統能效。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["A chip metric replaces facility energy measurement.","Chip, power delivery and cooling have separate efficiencies; chip performance is not system energy efficiency.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"芯片、供電與冷卻形成不同效率層；裸芯片性能不是完整系統能效。 把計算、通信與設施能量分別列表。","explanationEn":"Chip, power delivery and cooling have separate efficiencies; chip performance is not system energy efficiency. List compute, communication and facility energy separately."}},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"title":"冷卻與工作能量：證據驗證","titleEn":"Cooling and job energy: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-11"],"objective":"針對晶圓與設施散熱提出可反駁的冷卻與工作能量模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable cooling and job energy model and evidence record for wafer/facility cooling.","instruction":"沿用前一步「冷卻與工作能量」模型，檢查晶圓與設施散熱的兩個假想案例。把計算、通信與設施能量分別列表。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分芯片、供電與冷卻形成不同效率層；裸芯片性能不是完整系統能效。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous cooling and job energy model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving wafer/facility cooling. List compute, communication and facility energy separately. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Chip, power delivery and cooling have separate efficiencies; chip performance is not system energy efficiency.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"把計算、通信與設施能量分別列表。","observationEn":"List compute, communication and facility energy separately.","failure":"常見誤判：芯片指標即可取代設施能耗量測。","failureEn":"Common misconception: A chip metric replaces facility energy measurement.","check":"提交晶圓與設施散熱的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for wafer/facility cooling.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-12-k1","title":"冷卻與工作能量","titleEn":"Cooling and job energy","text":"芯片、供電與冷卻形成不同效率層；裸芯片性能不是完整系統能效。 本課架構對應：晶圓與設施散熱","textEn":"Chip, power delivery and cooling have separate efficiencies; chip performance is not system energy efficiency. Course architecture correspondence: Wafer/facility cooling","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-12-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"把計算、通信與設施能量分別列表。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；芯片指標即可取代設施能耗量測。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"List compute, communication and facility energy separately. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: A chip metric replaces facility energy measurement.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"]},{"id":"v11-cerebras-cs3-v11-12-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設算術強度 I=6 FLOP/byte、頻寬 B=0.9 TB/s、計算峯值 42 TFLOP/s，理想 roofline=min(42,I×B)=5.4 TFLOP/s。皆非產品規格，未含同步、精度轉換或工作形狀損失。","textEn":"Assume I=6 FLOP/byte, B=0.9 TB/s and compute peak 42 TFLOP/s: ideal roofline min(42,I×B)=5.4 TFLOP/s. These are not product specifications; synchronization, precision conversion and shape inefficiency are omitted.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras","v11x-cerebrasweight"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就晶圓與設施散熱的「冷卻與工作能量」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for cooling and job energy in wafer/facility cooling?","options":["芯片指標即可取代設施能耗量測。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","把計算、通信與設施能量分別列表。"],"optionsEn":["A chip metric replaces facility energy measurement.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","List compute, communication and facility energy separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"芯片、供電與冷卻形成不同效率層；裸芯片性能不是完整系統能效。 把計算、通信與設施能量分別列表。","explanationEn":"Chip, power delivery and cooling have separate efficiencies; chip performance is not system energy efficiency. List compute, communication and facility energy separately."}}]}],"summary":"以本地 SRAM、權重串流與晶圓尺度通信解析Cerebras CS-3 晶圓尺度叢集：六個原理與架構單元、十二項可保存的分析及驗證作業，附假想量化例、來源及衍生工程比較。","summaryEn":"Explore Cerebras CS-3 wafer-scale cluster through local sram, weight streaming and wafer-scale communication: six principle/architecture units and twelve saved analysis/validation tasks, with an assumed numerical example, primary sources and related engineering comparisons.","scope":"原創張量、運算成本及失效分析。架構圖是功能教學示意，非晶片floorplan或專有電路；數字為假想，需依精度、shape、資料分佈與系統邊界重算。","scopeEn":"Original tensor, compute-cost and failure analysis. Functional diagrams are not chip floorplans/proprietary circuits; assumed values need recalculation for precision, shape, data and boundaries.","workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"假設算術強度 I=6 FLOP/byte、頻寬 B=0.9 TB/s、計算峯值 42 TFLOP/s，理想 roofline=min(42,I×B)=5.4 TFLOP/s。皆非產品規格，未含同步、精度轉換或工作形狀損失。","textEn":"Assume I=6 FLOP/byte, B=0.9 TB/s and compute peak 42 TFLOP/s: ideal roofline min(42,I×B)=5.4 TFLOP/s. These are not product specifications; synchronization, precision conversion and shape inefficiency are omitted.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變模型邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are independently selected assumptions, not measured hardware, ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after boundary changes.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開架構及領域原理，不宣稱來源提供這組假想數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public architecture and principles, not these assumed measurements."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["WSE本地core與SRAM","MemoryX參數流","稀疏計算mapping","晶圓冗餘繞路","多CS系統梯度","晶圓與設施散熱"],"labelsEn":["WSE local cores and SRAM","MemoryX parameter streaming","Sparse compute mapping","Wafer redundancy and rerouting","Multi-CS system gradients","Wafer/facility cooling"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"vendorHints":[{"name":"Cerebras","nameEn":"Cerebras","url":"https://training-api.cerebras.ai/en/latest/wsc/Concepts/how-cerebras-works.html","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebras"]},{"name":"Cerebras","nameEn":"Cerebras","url":"https://www.cerebras.ai/blog/announcing-the-cerebras-architecture-for-extreme-scale-ai","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-cerebrasweight"]}],"architectureNodes":[["本地SRAM核心","Local-SRAM cores"],["晶圓網格","Wafer mesh"],["參數記憶體","Parameter memory"],["梯度聚合","Gradient aggregation"],["供電與冷卻","Power and cooling"]],"architectureEdges":[[2,0],[0,3],[3,2],[1,0],[0,1],[4,0]],"architectureFamily":"ai","educationEdition":11,"enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2","title":"Intel Loihi 2 脈衝計算平臺","titleEn":"Intel Loihi 2 spiking-compute platform","category":"computing","subcategory":"ai-neuromorphic","subcategoryTitle":"神經形態計算","subcategoryTitleEn":"Neuromorphic compute","learningTrack":"ai","learningSubdiscipline":"ai-neuromorphic","learningTags":["ai","ai-neuromorphic","intel-loihi2"],"kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"curriculumVersion":11,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":420,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"stages":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-stage1","order":1,"title":"系統邊界與基本原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and principles","description":"在Intel Loihi 2 脈衝計算平臺案例中比較graded spike事件與膜狀態微碼，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate graded-spike events and membrane-state microcode within the Intel Loihi 2 spiking-compute platform case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"title":"脈衝與時間編碼：架構分析","titleEn":"Spikes and temporal encoding: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"針對graded spike事件提出可反駁的脈衝與時間編碼模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable spikes and temporal encoding model and evidence record for graded-spike events.","instruction":"在「Intel Loihi 2 脈衝計算平臺」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識graded spike事件。神經形態計算以事件與狀態演化表達信息；脈衝頻率只是可能編碼之一。 建立脈衝與時間編碼的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是非同步事件、可程式神經元及本地突觸。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。比較頻率及事件時間對同一輸入的表示。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify graded-spike events in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Intel Loihi 2 spiking-compute platform. Neuromorphic computation uses events/state evolution; firing rate is one possible encoding. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of spikes and temporal encoding, focusing on asynchronous events, programmable neurons and local synapses. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Compare rate and event-time representations for one input. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"比較頻率及事件時間對同一輸入的表示。","observationEn":"Compare rate and event-time representations for one input.","failure":"常見誤判：脈衝網絡只能使用固定頻率編碼。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Spiking networks can use only fixed rate codes.","check":"提交graded spike事件的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for graded-spike events.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-01-k1","title":"脈衝與時間編碼","titleEn":"Spikes and temporal encoding","text":"神經形態計算以事件與狀態演化表達信息；脈衝頻率只是可能編碼之一。 本課架構對應：graded spike事件","textEn":"Neuromorphic computation uses events/state evolution; firing rate is one possible encoding. Course architecture correspondence: Graded-spike events","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-01-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較頻率及事件時間對同一輸入的表示。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；脈衝網絡只能使用固定頻率編碼。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare rate and event-time representations for one input. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Spiking networks can use only fixed rate codes.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-01-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設1000個神經元各平均10次/s，每事件成本20 nJ，核心事件能量率為1000×10×20 nJ/s=0.2 mW。未含閒置、輸入編碼、讀出與供電；不能當成Loihi實測或端到端功率。","textEn":"Assume 1000 neurons at 10 events/s with 20 nJ/event: event power is 0.2 mW. Idle, encoding, readout and supply are excluded; this is neither Loihi measurement nor end-to-end power.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就graded spike事件的「脈衝與時間編碼」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for spikes and temporal encoding in graded-spike events?","options":["神經形態計算以事件與狀態演化表達信息；脈衝頻率只是可能編碼之一。","脈衝網絡只能使用固定頻率編碼。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Neuromorphic computation uses events/state evolution; firing rate is one possible encoding.","Spiking networks can use only fixed rate codes.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"神經形態計算以事件與狀態演化表達信息；脈衝頻率只是可能編碼之一。 比較頻率及事件時間對同一輸入的表示。","explanationEn":"Neuromorphic computation uses events/state evolution; firing rate is one possible encoding. Compare rate and event-time representations for one input."}},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"title":"脈衝與時間編碼：證據驗證","titleEn":"Spikes and temporal encoding: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-intel-loihi2-v11-01"],"objective":"針對graded spike事件提出可反駁的脈衝與時間編碼模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable spikes and temporal encoding model and evidence record for graded-spike events.","instruction":"沿用前一步「脈衝與時間編碼」模型，檢查graded spike事件的兩個假想案例。比較頻率及事件時間對同一輸入的表示。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分神經形態計算以事件與狀態演化表達信息；脈衝頻率只是可能編碼之一。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous spikes and temporal encoding model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving graded-spike events. Compare rate and event-time representations for one input. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Neuromorphic computation uses events/state evolution; firing rate is one possible encoding.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"比較頻率及事件時間對同一輸入的表示。","observationEn":"Compare rate and event-time representations for one input.","failure":"常見誤判：脈衝網絡只能使用固定頻率編碼。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Spiking networks can use only fixed rate codes.","check":"提交graded spike事件的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for graded-spike events.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-02-k1","title":"脈衝與時間編碼","titleEn":"Spikes and temporal encoding","text":"神經形態計算以事件與狀態演化表達信息；脈衝頻率只是可能編碼之一。 本課架構對應：graded spike事件","textEn":"Neuromorphic computation uses events/state evolution; firing rate is one possible encoding. Course architecture correspondence: Graded-spike events","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-02-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較頻率及事件時間對同一輸入的表示。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；脈衝網絡只能使用固定頻率編碼。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare rate and event-time representations for one input. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Spiking networks can use only fixed rate codes.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-02-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設1000個神經元各平均10次/s，每事件成本20 nJ，核心事件能量率為1000×10×20 nJ/s=0.2 mW。未含閒置、輸入編碼、讀出與供電；不能當成Loihi實測或端到端功率。","textEn":"Assume 1000 neurons at 10 events/s with 20 nJ/event: event power is 0.2 mW. Idle, encoding, readout and supply are excluded; this is neither Loihi measurement nor end-to-end power.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就graded spike事件的「脈衝與時間編碼」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for spikes and temporal encoding in graded-spike events?","options":["脈衝網絡只能使用固定頻率編碼。","比較頻率及事件時間對同一輸入的表示。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Spiking networks can use only fixed rate codes.","Compare rate and event-time representations for one input.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"神經形態計算以事件與狀態演化表達信息；脈衝頻率只是可能編碼之一。 比較頻率及事件時間對同一輸入的表示。","explanationEn":"Neuromorphic computation uses events/state evolution; firing rate is one possible encoding. Compare rate and event-time representations for one input."}},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"title":"膜電位與閾值：架構分析","titleEn":"Membrane state and threshold: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-intel-loihi2-v11-02"],"objective":"針對膜狀態微碼提出可反駁的膜電位與閾值模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable membrane state and threshold model and evidence record for membrane-state microcode.","instruction":"在「Intel Loihi 2 脈衝計算平臺」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識膜狀態微碼。神經元模型積累、泄漏及發放；離散時間近似需要說明步長。 建立膜電位與閾值的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是非同步事件、可程式神經元及本地突觸。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。重算小型leaky積分模型與兩種步長誤差。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify membrane-state microcode in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Intel Loihi 2 spiking-compute platform. Neuron models accumulate, leak and fire; discrete approximations need timestep labels. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of membrane state and threshold, focusing on asynchronous events, programmable neurons and local synapses. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Recompute a leaky integrator with two timestep errors. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"重算小型leaky積分模型與兩種步長誤差。","observationEn":"Recompute a leaky integrator with two timestep errors.","failure":"常見誤判：改變時間步不會影響發放時間。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Changing timestep never affects firing time.","check":"提交膜狀態微碼的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for membrane-state microcode.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-03-k1","title":"膜電位與閾值","titleEn":"Membrane state and threshold","text":"神經元模型積累、泄漏及發放；離散時間近似需要說明步長。 本課架構對應：膜狀態微碼","textEn":"Neuron models accumulate, leak and fire; discrete approximations need timestep labels. Course architecture correspondence: Membrane-state microcode","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-03-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"重算小型leaky積分模型與兩種步長誤差。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；改變時間步不會影響發放時間。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recompute a leaky integrator with two timestep errors. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Changing timestep never affects firing time.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就膜狀態微碼的「膜電位與閾值」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for membrane state and threshold in membrane-state microcode?","options":["改變時間步不會影響發放時間。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","神經元模型積累、泄漏及發放；離散時間近似需要說明步長。"],"optionsEn":["Changing timestep never affects firing time.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Neuron models accumulate, leak and fire; discrete approximations need timestep labels."],"answer":2,"explanation":"神經元模型積累、泄漏及發放；離散時間近似需要說明步長。 重算小型leaky積分模型與兩種步長誤差。","explanationEn":"Neuron models accumulate, leak and fire; discrete approximations need timestep labels. Recompute a leaky integrator with two timestep errors."}},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"title":"膜電位與閾值：證據驗證","titleEn":"Membrane state and threshold: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-intel-loihi2-v11-03"],"objective":"針對膜狀態微碼提出可反駁的膜電位與閾值模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable membrane state and threshold model and evidence record for membrane-state microcode.","instruction":"沿用前一步「膜電位與閾值」模型，檢查膜狀態微碼的兩個假想案例。重算小型leaky積分模型與兩種步長誤差。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分神經元模型積累、泄漏及發放；離散時間近似需要說明步長。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous membrane state and threshold model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving membrane-state microcode. Recompute a leaky integrator with two timestep errors. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Neuron models accumulate, leak and fire; discrete approximations need timestep labels.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"重算小型leaky積分模型與兩種步長誤差。","observationEn":"Recompute a leaky integrator with two timestep errors.","failure":"常見誤判：改變時間步不會影響發放時間。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Changing timestep never affects firing time.","check":"提交膜狀態微碼的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for membrane-state microcode.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-04-k1","title":"膜電位與閾值","titleEn":"Membrane state and threshold","text":"神經元模型積累、泄漏及發放；離散時間近似需要說明步長。 本課架構對應：膜狀態微碼","textEn":"Neuron models accumulate, leak and fire; discrete approximations need timestep labels. Course architecture correspondence: Membrane-state microcode","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-04-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"重算小型leaky積分模型與兩種步長誤差。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；改變時間步不會影響發放時間。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recompute a leaky integrator with two timestep errors. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Changing timestep never affects firing time.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就膜狀態微碼的「膜電位與閾值」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for membrane state and threshold in membrane-state microcode?","options":["重算小型leaky積分模型與兩種步長誤差。","改變時間步不會影響發放時間。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Recompute a leaky integrator with two timestep errors.","Changing timestep never affects firing time.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"神經元模型積累、泄漏及發放；離散時間近似需要說明步長。 重算小型leaky積分模型與兩種步長誤差。","explanationEn":"Neuron models accumulate, leak and fire; discrete approximations need timestep labels. Recompute a leaky integrator with two timestep errors."}}]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-stage2","order":2,"title":"功能架構與量化模型","titleEn":"Functional architecture and quantitative models","description":"在Intel Loihi 2 脈衝計算平臺案例中比較local synapse與學習與NoC事件突發，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate local synapses and learning and noc event bursts within the Intel Loihi 2 spiking-compute platform case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"title":"突觸記憶與可塑性：架構分析","titleEn":"Synaptic memory and plasticity: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-intel-loihi2-v11-04"],"objective":"針對local synapse與學習提出可反駁的突觸記憶與可塑性模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable synaptic memory and plasticity model and evidence record for local synapses and learning.","instruction":"在「Intel Loihi 2 脈衝計算平臺」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識local synapse與學習。權重及學習規則儲存在本地狀態；在線學習與推論模式有不同數據流。 建立突觸記憶與可塑性的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是非同步事件、可程式神經元及本地突觸。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。分開權重讀、狀態寫與學習更新事件。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify local synapses and learning in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Intel Loihi 2 spiking-compute platform. Local state holds weights/rules; learning and inference have different flows. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of synaptic memory and plasticity, focusing on asynchronous events, programmable neurons and local synapses. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Separate weight reads, state writes and learning updates. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"分開權重讀、狀態寫與學習更新事件。","observationEn":"Separate weight reads, state writes and learning updates.","failure":"常見誤判：神經形態推論會自動完成所有監督學習。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Neuromorphic inference automatically performs all supervised learning.","check":"提交local synapse與學習的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for local synapses and learning.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-05-k1","title":"突觸記憶與可塑性","titleEn":"Synaptic memory and plasticity","text":"權重及學習規則儲存在本地狀態；在線學習與推論模式有不同數據流。 本課架構對應：local synapse與學習","textEn":"Local state holds weights/rules; learning and inference have different flows. Course architecture correspondence: Local synapses and learning","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-05-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"分開權重讀、狀態寫與學習更新事件。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；神經形態推論會自動完成所有監督學習。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Separate weight reads, state writes and learning updates. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Neuromorphic inference automatically performs all supervised learning.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就local synapse與學習的「突觸記憶與可塑性」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for synaptic memory and plasticity in local synapses and learning?","options":["神經形態推論會自動完成所有監督學習。","權重及學習規則儲存在本地狀態；在線學習與推論模式有不同數據流。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Neuromorphic inference automatically performs all supervised learning.","Local state holds weights/rules; learning and inference have different flows.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"權重及學習規則儲存在本地狀態；在線學習與推論模式有不同數據流。 分開權重讀、狀態寫與學習更新事件。","explanationEn":"Local state holds weights/rules; learning and inference have different flows. Separate weight reads, state writes and learning updates."}},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"title":"突觸記憶與可塑性：證據驗證","titleEn":"Synaptic memory and plasticity: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-intel-loihi2-v11-05"],"objective":"針對local synapse與學習提出可反駁的突觸記憶與可塑性模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable synaptic memory and plasticity model and evidence record for local synapses and learning.","instruction":"沿用前一步「突觸記憶與可塑性」模型，檢查local synapse與學習的兩個假想案例。分開權重讀、狀態寫與學習更新事件。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分權重及學習規則儲存在本地狀態；在線學習與推論模式有不同數據流。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous synaptic memory and plasticity model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving local synapses and learning. Separate weight reads, state writes and learning updates. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Local state holds weights/rules; learning and inference have different flows.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"分開權重讀、狀態寫與學習更新事件。","observationEn":"Separate weight reads, state writes and learning updates.","failure":"常見誤判：神經形態推論會自動完成所有監督學習。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Neuromorphic inference automatically performs all supervised learning.","check":"提交local synapse與學習的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for local synapses and learning.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-06-k1","title":"突觸記憶與可塑性","titleEn":"Synaptic memory and plasticity","text":"權重及學習規則儲存在本地狀態；在線學習與推論模式有不同數據流。 本課架構對應：local synapse與學習","textEn":"Local state holds weights/rules; learning and inference have different flows. Course architecture correspondence: Local synapses and learning","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-06-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"分開權重讀、狀態寫與學習更新事件。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；神經形態推論會自動完成所有監督學習。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Separate weight reads, state writes and learning updates. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Neuromorphic inference automatically performs all supervised learning.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就local synapse與學習的「突觸記憶與可塑性」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for synaptic memory and plasticity in local synapses and learning?","options":["神經形態推論會自動完成所有監督學習。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","分開權重讀、狀態寫與學習更新事件。"],"optionsEn":["Neuromorphic inference automatically performs all supervised learning.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Separate weight reads, state writes and learning updates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"權重及學習規則儲存在本地狀態；在線學習與推論模式有不同數據流。 分開權重讀、狀態寫與學習更新事件。","explanationEn":"Local state holds weights/rules; learning and inference have different flows. Separate weight reads, state writes and learning updates."}},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"title":"事件網路與擁塞：架構分析","titleEn":"Event networks and congestion: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-intel-loihi2-v11-06"],"objective":"針對NoC事件突發提出可反駁的事件網路與擁塞模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable event networks and congestion model and evidence record for noc event bursts.","instruction":"在「Intel Loihi 2 脈衝計算平臺」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識NoC事件突發。稀疏事件減少部分活動，但突發相關放電可能使NoC擁塞。 建立事件網路與擁塞的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是非同步事件、可程式神經元及本地突觸。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。用平均及突發事件流比較峯值隊列。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify noc event bursts in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Intel Loihi 2 spiking-compute platform. Sparse events reduce some activity; correlated bursts may congest the NoC. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of event networks and congestion, focusing on asynchronous events, programmable neurons and local synapses. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Compare peak queues under mean/bursty event flows. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"用平均及突發事件流比較峯值隊列。","observationEn":"Compare peak queues under mean/bursty event flows.","failure":"常見誤判：低平均放電率保證永不擁塞。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low mean firing guarantees no congestion.","check":"提交NoC事件突發的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for noc event bursts.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-07-k1","title":"事件網路與擁塞","titleEn":"Event networks and congestion","text":"稀疏事件減少部分活動，但突發相關放電可能使NoC擁塞。 本課架構對應：NoC事件突發","textEn":"Sparse events reduce some activity; correlated bursts may congest the NoC. Course architecture correspondence: NoC event bursts","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-07-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"用平均及突發事件流比較峯值隊列。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低平均放電率保證永不擁塞。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare peak queues under mean/bursty event flows. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low mean firing guarantees no congestion.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就NoC事件突發的「事件網路與擁塞」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for event networks and congestion in noc event bursts?","options":["稀疏事件減少部分活動，但突發相關放電可能使NoC擁塞。","低平均放電率保證永不擁塞。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Sparse events reduce some activity; correlated bursts may congest the NoC.","Low mean firing guarantees no congestion.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"稀疏事件減少部分活動，但突發相關放電可能使NoC擁塞。 用平均及突發事件流比較峯值隊列。","explanationEn":"Sparse events reduce some activity; correlated bursts may congest the NoC. Compare peak queues under mean/bursty event flows."}},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"title":"事件網路與擁塞：證據驗證","titleEn":"Event networks and congestion: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-intel-loihi2-v11-07"],"objective":"針對NoC事件突發提出可反駁的事件網路與擁塞模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable event networks and congestion model and evidence record for noc event bursts.","instruction":"沿用前一步「事件網路與擁塞」模型，檢查NoC事件突發的兩個假想案例。用平均及突發事件流比較峯值隊列。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分稀疏事件減少部分活動，但突發相關放電可能使NoC擁塞。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous event networks and congestion model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving noc event bursts. Compare peak queues under mean/bursty event flows. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Sparse events reduce some activity; correlated bursts may congest the NoC.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"用平均及突發事件流比較峯值隊列。","observationEn":"Compare peak queues under mean/bursty event flows.","failure":"常見誤判：低平均放電率保證永不擁塞。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low mean firing guarantees no congestion.","check":"提交NoC事件突發的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for noc event bursts.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-08-k1","title":"事件網路與擁塞","titleEn":"Event networks and congestion","text":"稀疏事件減少部分活動，但突發相關放電可能使NoC擁塞。 本課架構對應：NoC事件突發","textEn":"Sparse events reduce some activity; correlated bursts may congest the NoC. Course architecture correspondence: NoC event bursts","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-08-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"用平均及突發事件流比較峯值隊列。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低平均放電率保證永不擁塞。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare peak queues under mean/bursty event flows. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low mean firing guarantees no congestion.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就NoC事件突發的「事件網路與擁塞」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for event networks and congestion in noc event bursts?","options":["低平均放電率保證永不擁塞。","用平均及突發事件流比較峯值隊列。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Low mean firing guarantees no congestion.","Compare peak queues under mean/bursty event flows.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"稀疏事件減少部分活動，但突發相關放電可能使NoC擁塞。 用平均及突發事件流比較峯值隊列。","explanationEn":"Sparse events reduce some activity; correlated bursts may congest the NoC. Compare peak queues under mean/bursty event flows."}}]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-stage3","order":3,"title":"獨立驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Independent validation and engineering handoff","description":"在Intel Loihi 2 脈衝計算平臺案例中比較可程式模型映射與Lava端到端比較，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate programmable model mapping and lava end-to-end comparison within the Intel Loihi 2 spiking-compute platform case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"title":"可程式神經元：架構分析","titleEn":"Programmable neurons: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-intel-loihi2-v11-08"],"objective":"針對可程式模型映射提出可反駁的可程式神經元模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable programmable neurons model and evidence record for programmable model mapping.","instruction":"在「Intel Loihi 2 脈衝計算平臺」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識可程式模型映射。可編程模型擴展神經元行爲，但支持指令、精度與存儲仍限制模型。 建立可程式神經元的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是非同步事件、可程式神經元及本地突觸。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。將數學神經元映射至允許的基本操作。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify programmable model mapping in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Intel Loihi 2 spiking-compute platform. Programmability expands behavior within instruction, precision and memory limits. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of programmable neurons, focusing on asynchronous events, programmable neurons and local synapses. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Map a mathematical neuron to allowed primitives. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"將數學神經元映射至允許的基本操作。","observationEn":"Map a mathematical neuron to allowed primitives.","failure":"常見誤判：可編程就是無精度與容量邊界。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Programmable means no precision or capacity limits.","check":"提交可程式模型映射的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for programmable model mapping.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-09-k1","title":"可程式神經元","titleEn":"Programmable neurons","text":"可編程模型擴展神經元行爲，但支持指令、精度與存儲仍限制模型。 本課架構對應：可程式模型映射","textEn":"Programmability expands behavior within instruction, precision and memory limits. Course architecture correspondence: Programmable model mapping","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-09-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"將數學神經元映射至允許的基本操作。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；可編程就是無精度與容量邊界。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Map a mathematical neuron to allowed primitives. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Programmable means no precision or capacity limits.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就可程式模型映射的「可程式神經元」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for programmable neurons in programmable model mapping?","options":["可編程就是無精度與容量邊界。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","可編程模型擴展神經元行爲，但支持指令、精度與存儲仍限制模型。"],"optionsEn":["Programmable means no precision or capacity limits.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Programmability expands behavior within instruction, precision and memory limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可編程模型擴展神經元行爲，但支持指令、精度與存儲仍限制模型。 將數學神經元映射至允許的基本操作。","explanationEn":"Programmability expands behavior within instruction, precision and memory limits. Map a mathematical neuron to allowed primitives."}},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"title":"可程式神經元：證據驗證","titleEn":"Programmable neurons: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-intel-loihi2-v11-09"],"objective":"針對可程式模型映射提出可反駁的可程式神經元模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable programmable neurons model and evidence record for programmable model mapping.","instruction":"沿用前一步「可程式神經元」模型，檢查可程式模型映射的兩個假想案例。將數學神經元映射至允許的基本操作。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分可編程模型擴展神經元行爲，但支持指令、精度與存儲仍限制模型。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous programmable neurons model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving programmable model mapping. Map a mathematical neuron to allowed primitives. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Programmability expands behavior within instruction, precision and memory limits.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"將數學神經元映射至允許的基本操作。","observationEn":"Map a mathematical neuron to allowed primitives.","failure":"常見誤判：可編程就是無精度與容量邊界。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Programmable means no precision or capacity limits.","check":"提交可程式模型映射的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for programmable model mapping.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-10-k1","title":"可程式神經元","titleEn":"Programmable neurons","text":"可編程模型擴展神經元行爲，但支持指令、精度與存儲仍限制模型。 本課架構對應：可程式模型映射","textEn":"Programmability expands behavior within instruction, precision and memory limits. Course architecture correspondence: Programmable model mapping","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-10-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"將數學神經元映射至允許的基本操作。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；可編程就是無精度與容量邊界。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Map a mathematical neuron to allowed primitives. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Programmable means no precision or capacity limits.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就可程式模型映射的「可程式神經元」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for programmable neurons in programmable model mapping?","options":["將數學神經元映射至允許的基本操作。","可編程就是無精度與容量邊界。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Map a mathematical neuron to allowed primitives.","Programmable means no precision or capacity limits.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"可編程模型擴展神經元行爲，但支持指令、精度與存儲仍限制模型。 將數學神經元映射至允許的基本操作。","explanationEn":"Programmability expands behavior within instruction, precision and memory limits. Map a mathematical neuron to allowed primitives."}},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"title":"效率與公平比較：架構分析","titleEn":"Efficiency and fair comparison: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-intel-loihi2-v11-10"],"objective":"針對Lava端到端比較提出可反駁的效率與公平比較模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable efficiency and fair comparison model and evidence record for lava end-to-end comparison.","instruction":"在「Intel Loihi 2 脈衝計算平臺」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識Lava端到端比較。事件驅動能耗須連同輸入編碼與結果質量比較；與密集網絡需相同任務邊界。 建立效率與公平比較的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是非同步事件、可程式神經元及本地突觸。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。比較全流程時間、能量與準確率而非只計芯片核心。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify lava end-to-end comparison in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Intel Loihi 2 spiking-compute platform. Event-driven energy needs encoding/result-quality context; dense-network comparison needs matching task boundaries. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of efficiency and fair comparison, focusing on asynchronous events, programmable neurons and local synapses. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Compare end-to-end time, energy and accuracy beyond cores. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"比較全流程時間、能量與準確率而非只計芯片核心。","observationEn":"Compare end-to-end time, energy and accuracy beyond cores.","failure":"常見誤判：事件稀疏本身就證明所有任務更省電。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Sparse events alone prove lower energy for every task.","check":"提交Lava端到端比較的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for lava end-to-end comparison.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-11-k1","title":"效率與公平比較","titleEn":"Efficiency and fair comparison","text":"事件驅動能耗須連同輸入編碼與結果質量比較；與密集網絡需相同任務邊界。 本課架構對應：Lava端到端比較","textEn":"Event-driven energy needs encoding/result-quality context; dense-network comparison needs matching task boundaries. Course architecture correspondence: Lava end-to-end comparison","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-11-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較全流程時間、能量與準確率而非只計芯片核心。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；事件稀疏本身就證明所有任務更省電。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare end-to-end time, energy and accuracy beyond cores. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Sparse events alone prove lower energy for every task.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-11-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設1000個神經元各平均10次/s，每事件成本20 nJ，核心事件能量率為1000×10×20 nJ/s=0.2 mW。未含閒置、輸入編碼、讀出與供電；不能當成Loihi實測或端到端功率。","textEn":"Assume 1000 neurons at 10 events/s with 20 nJ/event: event power is 0.2 mW. Idle, encoding, readout and supply are excluded; this is neither Loihi measurement nor end-to-end power.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就Lava端到端比較的「效率與公平比較」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for efficiency and fair comparison in lava end-to-end comparison?","options":["事件稀疏本身就證明所有任務更省電。","事件驅動能耗須連同輸入編碼與結果質量比較；與密集網絡需相同任務邊界。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Sparse events alone prove lower energy for every task.","Event-driven energy needs encoding/result-quality context; dense-network comparison needs matching task boundaries.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"事件驅動能耗須連同輸入編碼與結果質量比較；與密集網絡需相同任務邊界。 比較全流程時間、能量與準確率而非只計芯片核心。","explanationEn":"Event-driven energy needs encoding/result-quality context; dense-network comparison needs matching task boundaries. Compare end-to-end time, energy and accuracy beyond cores."}},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"title":"效率與公平比較：證據驗證","titleEn":"Efficiency and fair comparison: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-intel-loihi2-v11-11"],"objective":"針對Lava端到端比較提出可反駁的效率與公平比較模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable efficiency and fair comparison model and evidence record for lava end-to-end comparison.","instruction":"沿用前一步「效率與公平比較」模型，檢查Lava端到端比較的兩個假想案例。比較全流程時間、能量與準確率而非只計芯片核心。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分事件驅動能耗須連同輸入編碼與結果質量比較；與密集網絡需相同任務邊界。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous efficiency and fair comparison model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving lava end-to-end comparison. Compare end-to-end time, energy and accuracy beyond cores. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Event-driven energy needs encoding/result-quality context; dense-network comparison needs matching task boundaries.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"比較全流程時間、能量與準確率而非只計芯片核心。","observationEn":"Compare end-to-end time, energy and accuracy beyond cores.","failure":"常見誤判：事件稀疏本身就證明所有任務更省電。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Sparse events alone prove lower energy for every task.","check":"提交Lava端到端比較的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for lava end-to-end comparison.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-12-k1","title":"效率與公平比較","titleEn":"Efficiency and fair comparison","text":"事件驅動能耗須連同輸入編碼與結果質量比較；與密集網絡需相同任務邊界。 本課架構對應：Lava端到端比較","textEn":"Event-driven energy needs encoding/result-quality context; dense-network comparison needs matching task boundaries. Course architecture correspondence: Lava end-to-end comparison","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-12-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較全流程時間、能量與準確率而非只計芯片核心。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；事件稀疏本身就證明所有任務更省電。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare end-to-end time, energy and accuracy beyond cores. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Sparse events alone prove lower energy for every task.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"]},{"id":"v11-intel-loihi2-v11-12-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設1000個神經元各平均10次/s，每事件成本20 nJ，核心事件能量率為1000×10×20 nJ/s=0.2 mW。未含閒置、輸入編碼、讀出與供電；不能當成Loihi實測或端到端功率。","textEn":"Assume 1000 neurons at 10 events/s with 20 nJ/event: event power is 0.2 mW. Idle, encoding, readout and supply are excluded; this is neither Loihi measurement nor end-to-end power.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi","v11x-neuromorphic"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就Lava端到端比較的「效率與公平比較」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for efficiency and fair comparison in lava end-to-end comparison?","options":["事件稀疏本身就證明所有任務更省電。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","比較全流程時間、能量與準確率而非只計芯片核心。"],"optionsEn":["Sparse events alone prove lower energy for every task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Compare end-to-end time, energy and accuracy beyond cores."],"answer":2,"explanation":"事件驅動能耗須連同輸入編碼與結果質量比較；與密集網絡需相同任務邊界。 比較全流程時間、能量與準確率而非只計芯片核心。","explanationEn":"Event-driven energy needs encoding/result-quality context; dense-network comparison needs matching task boundaries. Compare end-to-end time, energy and accuracy beyond cores."}}]}],"summary":"以非同步事件、可程式神經元及本地突觸解析Intel Loihi 2 脈衝計算平臺：六個原理與架構單元、十二項可保存的分析及驗證作業，附假想量化例、來源及衍生工程比較。","summaryEn":"Explore Intel Loihi 2 spiking-compute platform through asynchronous events, programmable neurons and local synapses: six principle/architecture units and twelve saved analysis/validation tasks, with an assumed numerical example, primary sources and related engineering comparisons.","scope":"原創張量、運算成本及失效分析。架構圖是功能教學示意，非晶片floorplan或專有電路；數字為假想，需依精度、shape、資料分佈與系統邊界重算。","scopeEn":"Original tensor, compute-cost and failure analysis. Functional diagrams are not chip floorplans/proprietary circuits; assumed values need recalculation for precision, shape, data and boundaries.","workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"假設1000個神經元各平均10次/s，每事件成本20 nJ，核心事件能量率為1000×10×20 nJ/s=0.2 mW。未含閒置、輸入編碼、讀出與供電；不能當成Loihi實測或端到端功率。","textEn":"Assume 1000 neurons at 10 events/s with 20 nJ/event: event power is 0.2 mW. Idle, encoding, readout and supply are excluded; this is neither Loihi measurement nor end-to-end power.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變模型邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are independently selected assumptions, not measured hardware, ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after boundary changes.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開架構及領域原理，不宣稱來源提供這組假想數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public architecture and principles, not these assumed measurements."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["graded spike事件","膜狀態微碼","local synapse與學習","NoC事件突發","可程式模型映射","Lava端到端比較"],"labelsEn":["Graded-spike events","Membrane-state microcode","Local synapses and learning","NoC event bursts","Programmable model mapping","Lava end-to-end comparison"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"vendorHints":[{"name":"Intel","nameEn":"Intel","url":"https://www.intel.com/content/dam/www/central-libraries/us/en/documents/neuromorphic-computing-loihi-2-brief.pdf","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-loihi"]},{"name":"Intel","nameEn":"Intel","url":"https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/research/neuromorphic-computing.html","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-neuromorphic"]}],"architectureNodes":[["事件編碼器","Event encoder"],["可程式神經元","Programmable neurons"],["本地突觸","Local synapses"],["事件NoC","Event NoC"],["輸出解碼器","Output decoder"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,1],[1,3],[3,1],[3,4]],"architectureFamily":"ai","educationEdition":11,"enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100","title":"NVIDIA DGX H100 八 GPU 伺服器","titleEn":"NVIDIA DGX H100 eight-GPU server","category":"computing","subcategory":"server-design","subcategoryTitle":"伺服器平臺工程","subcategoryTitleEn":"Server-platform engineering","learningTrack":"servers","learningSubdiscipline":"server-design","learningTags":["servers","server-design","dgx-h100"],"kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"curriculumVersion":11,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":420,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"stages":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-stage1","order":1,"title":"系統邊界與基本原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and principles","description":"在NVIDIA DGX H100 八 GPU 伺服器案例中比較H100與主記憶拓撲與NVSwitch與外部NIC，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate h100 and host-memory topology and nvswitch and external nics within the NVIDIA DGX H100 eight-GPU server case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：架構分析","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"針對H100與主記憶拓撲提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for h100 and host-memory topology.","instruction":"在「NVIDIA DGX H100 八 GPU 伺服器」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識H100與主記憶拓撲。CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 建立節點與記憶體層級的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是雙 CPU、NVSwitch 與計算／儲存網路分層。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify h100 and host-memory topology in the mentor diagram and primary sources for NVIDIA DGX H100 eight-GPU server. CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of nodes and memory hierarchy, focusing on dual cpus, nvswitch and compute/storage fabric layers. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交H100與主記憶拓撲的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for h100 and host-memory topology.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-01-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：H100與主記憶拓撲","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: H100 and host-memory topology","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-01-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-01-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.020，使用 8 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=7.0175。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.020 and 8 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=7.0175. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就H100與主記憶拓撲的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in h100 and host-memory topology?","options":["CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。","統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.","Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：證據驗證","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-dgx-h100-v11-01"],"objective":"針對H100與主記憶拓撲提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for h100 and host-memory topology.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點與記憶體層級」模型，檢查H100與主記憶拓撲的兩個假想案例。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous nodes and memory hierarchy model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving h100 and host-memory topology. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交H100與主記憶拓撲的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for h100 and host-memory topology.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-02-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：H100與主記憶拓撲","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: H100 and host-memory topology","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-02-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-02-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.020，使用 8 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=7.0175。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.020 and 8 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=7.0175. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就H100與主記憶拓撲的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in h100 and host-memory topology?","options":["統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：架構分析","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-dgx-h100-v11-02"],"objective":"針對NVSwitch與外部NIC提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for nvswitch and external nics.","instruction":"在「NVIDIA DGX H100 八 GPU 伺服器」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識NVSwitch與外部NIC。高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 建立節點內與節點間網路的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是雙 CPU、NVSwitch 與計算／儲存網路分層。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify nvswitch and external nics in the mentor diagram and primary sources for NVIDIA DGX H100 eight-GPU server. Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of intranode and internode networks, focusing on dual cpus, nvswitch and compute/storage fabric layers. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交NVSwitch與外部NIC的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for nvswitch and external nics.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-03-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：NVSwitch與外部NIC","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: NVSwitch and external NICs","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-03-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就NVSwitch與外部NIC的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in nvswitch and external nics?","options":["節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。"],"optionsEn":["Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：證據驗證","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-dgx-h100-v11-03"],"objective":"針對NVSwitch與外部NIC提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for nvswitch and external nics.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點內與節點間網路」模型，檢查NVSwitch與外部NIC的兩個假想案例。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous intranode and internode networks model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving nvswitch and external nics. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交NVSwitch與外部NIC的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for nvswitch and external nics.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-04-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：NVSwitch與外部NIC","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: NVSwitch and external NICs","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-04-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就NVSwitch與外部NIC的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in nvswitch and external nics?","options":["按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}}]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-stage2","order":2,"title":"功能架構與量化模型","titleEn":"Functional architecture and quantitative models","description":"在NVIDIA DGX H100 八 GPU 伺服器案例中比較八GPU工作切分與NVMe與檢查點，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate eight-gpu work partition and nvme and checkpoints within the NVIDIA DGX H100 eight-GPU server case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：架構分析","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-dgx-h100-v11-04"],"objective":"針對八GPU工作切分提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for eight-gpu work partition.","instruction":"在「NVIDIA DGX H100 八 GPU 伺服器」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識八GPU工作切分。串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 建立工作分割與平行效率的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是雙 CPU、NVSwitch 與計算／儲存網路分層。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify eight-gpu work partition in the mentor diagram and primary sources for NVIDIA DGX H100 eight-GPU server. Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of work partition and parallel efficiency, focusing on dual cpus, nvswitch and compute/storage fabric layers. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交八GPU工作切分的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for eight-gpu work partition.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-05-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：八GPU工作切分","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: Eight-GPU work partition","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-05-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就八GPU工作切分的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in eight-gpu work partition?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：證據驗證","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-dgx-h100-v11-05"],"objective":"針對八GPU工作切分提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for eight-gpu work partition.","instruction":"沿用前一步「工作分割與平行效率」模型，檢查八GPU工作切分的兩個假想案例。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous work partition and parallel efficiency model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving eight-gpu work partition. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交八GPU工作切分的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for eight-gpu work partition.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-06-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：八GPU工作切分","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: Eight-GPU work partition","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-06-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就八GPU工作切分的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in eight-gpu work partition?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."],"answer":2,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：架構分析","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-dgx-h100-v11-06"],"objective":"針對NVMe與檢查點提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for nvme and checkpoints.","instruction":"在「NVIDIA DGX H100 八 GPU 伺服器」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識NVMe與檢查點。暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 建立儲存階層與檢查點的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是雙 CPU、NVSwitch 與計算／儲存網路分層。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify nvme and checkpoints in the mentor diagram and primary sources for NVIDIA DGX H100 eight-GPU server. Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of storage tiers and checkpoints, focusing on dual cpus, nvswitch and compute/storage fabric layers. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交NVMe與檢查點的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for nvme and checkpoints.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-07-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：NVMe與檢查點","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: NVMe and checkpoints","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-07-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就NVMe與檢查點的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in nvme and checkpoints?","options":["暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。","容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.","Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：證據驗證","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-dgx-h100-v11-07"],"objective":"針對NVMe與檢查點提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for nvme and checkpoints.","instruction":"沿用前一步「儲存階層與檢查點」模型，檢查NVMe與檢查點的兩個假想案例。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous storage tiers and checkpoints model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving nvme and checkpoints. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交NVMe與檢查點的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for nvme and checkpoints.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-08-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：NVMe與檢查點","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: NVMe and checkpoints","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-08-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就NVMe與檢查點的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in nvme and checkpoints?","options":["容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}}]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-stage3","order":3,"title":"獨立驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Independent validation and engineering handoff","description":"在NVIDIA DGX H100 八 GPU 伺服器案例中比較PSU冗餘與風冷與BMC與作業復原，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate psu redundancy and air cooling and bmc and job recovery within the NVIDIA DGX H100 eight-GPU server case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：架構分析","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-dgx-h100-v11-08"],"objective":"針對PSU冗餘與風冷提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for psu redundancy and air cooling.","instruction":"在「NVIDIA DGX H100 八 GPU 伺服器」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識PSU冗餘與風冷。設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 建立供電冷卻與設施的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是雙 CPU、NVSwitch 與計算／儲存網路分層。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify psu redundancy and air cooling in the mentor diagram and primary sources for NVIDIA DGX H100 eight-GPU server. Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of power, cooling and facilities, focusing on dual cpus, nvswitch and compute/storage fabric layers. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交PSU冗餘與風冷的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for psu redundancy and air cooling.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-09-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：PSU冗餘與風冷","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: PSU redundancy and air cooling","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-09-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就PSU冗餘與風冷的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in psu redundancy and air cooling?","options":["低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。"],"optionsEn":["Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：證據驗證","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-dgx-h100-v11-09"],"objective":"針對PSU冗餘與風冷提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for psu redundancy and air cooling.","instruction":"沿用前一步「供電冷卻與設施」模型，檢查PSU冗餘與風冷的兩個假想案例。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous power, cooling and facilities model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving psu redundancy and air cooling. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交PSU冗餘與風冷的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for psu redundancy and air cooling.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-10-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：PSU冗餘與風冷","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: PSU redundancy and air cooling","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-10-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就PSU冗餘與風冷的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in psu redundancy and air cooling?","options":["覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"title":"排程隔離與復原：架構分析","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-dgx-h100-v11-10"],"objective":"針對BMC與作業復原提出可反駁的排程隔離與復原模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable scheduling, isolation and recovery model and evidence record for bmc and job recovery.","instruction":"在「NVIDIA DGX H100 八 GPU 伺服器」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識BMC與作業復原。多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 建立排程隔離與復原的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是雙 CPU、NVSwitch 與計算／儲存網路分層。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify bmc and job recovery in the mentor diagram and primary sources for NVIDIA DGX H100 eight-GPU server. Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of scheduling, isolation and recovery, focusing on dual cpus, nvswitch and compute/storage fabric layers. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","observationEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table.","failure":"常見誤判：換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","check":"提交BMC與作業復原的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for bmc and job recovery.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-11-k1","title":"排程隔離與復原","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery","text":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 本課架構對應：BMC與作業復原","textEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Course architecture correspondence: BMC and job recovery","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-11-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-11-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.020，使用 8 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=7.0175。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.020 and 8 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=7.0175. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就BMC與作業復原的「排程隔離與復原」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for scheduling, isolation and recovery in bmc and job recovery?","options":["換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","explanationEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."}},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"title":"排程隔離與復原：證據驗證","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-dgx-h100-v11-11"],"objective":"針對BMC與作業復原提出可反駁的排程隔離與復原模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable scheduling, isolation and recovery model and evidence record for bmc and job recovery.","instruction":"沿用前一步「排程隔離與復原」模型，檢查BMC與作業復原的兩個假想案例。在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous scheduling, isolation and recovery model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving bmc and job recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","observationEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table.","failure":"常見誤判：換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","check":"提交BMC與作業復原的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for bmc and job recovery.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-12-k1","title":"排程隔離與復原","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery","text":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 本課架構對應：BMC與作業復原","textEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Course architecture correspondence: BMC and job recovery","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-12-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-dgx-h100-v11-12-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.020，使用 8 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=7.0175。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.020 and 8 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=7.0175. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx","v11x-cuda"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就BMC與作業復原的「排程隔離與復原」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for scheduling, isolation and recovery in bmc and job recovery?","options":["換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","explanationEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."}}]}],"summary":"以雙 CPU、NVSwitch 與計算／儲存網路分層解析NVIDIA DGX H100 八 GPU 伺服器：六個原理與架構單元、十二項可保存的分析及驗證作業，附假想量化例、來源及衍生工程比較。","summaryEn":"Explore NVIDIA DGX H100 eight-GPU server through dual cpus, nvswitch and compute/storage fabric layers: six principle/architecture units and twelve saved analysis/validation tasks, with an assumed numerical example, primary sources and related engineering comparisons.","scope":"公開伺服器與超算架構的離線工作流、通信、儲存及能量模型；非機櫃接線、供電施工或實體維護SOP，也不表示學員取得廠商／研究中心設備存取。","scopeEn":"Offline workflow, fabric, storage and energy models of public servers/HPC. No rack-wiring, power-installation or physical-maintenance SOP and no vendor/research-center hardware access is implied.","workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.020，使用 8 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=7.0175。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.020 and 8 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=7.0175. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變模型邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are independently selected assumptions, not measured hardware, ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after boundary changes.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開架構及領域原理，不宣稱來源提供這組假想數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public architecture and principles, not these assumed measurements."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["H100與主記憶拓撲","NVSwitch與外部NIC","八GPU工作切分","NVMe與檢查點","PSU冗餘與風冷","BMC與作業復原"],"labelsEn":["H100 and host-memory topology","NVSwitch and external NICs","Eight-GPU work partition","NVMe and checkpoints","PSU redundancy and air cooling","BMC and job recovery"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"vendorHints":[{"name":"NVIDIA","nameEn":"NVIDIA","url":"https://docs.nvidia.com/dgx/dgxh100-user-guide/introduction-to-dgxh100.html","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-dgx"]},{"name":"NVIDIA","nameEn":"NVIDIA","url":"https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-c-programming-guide/","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-cuda"]}],"architectureNodes":[["計算節點","Compute nodes"],["本地記憶體","Local memory"],["叢集網路","Cluster fabric"],["儲存階層","Storage tiers"],["供電與冷卻","Power and cooling"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[0,2],[2,3],[4,0]],"architectureFamily":"server","educationEdition":11,"enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72","title":"NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 機架系統","titleEn":"NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 rack system","category":"computing","subcategory":"server-design","subcategoryTitle":"伺服器平臺工程","subcategoryTitleEn":"Server-platform engineering","learningTrack":"servers","learningSubdiscipline":"server-design","learningTags":["servers","server-design","gb200-nvl72"],"kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"curriculumVersion":11,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":420,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"stages":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-stage1","order":1,"title":"系統邊界與基本原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and principles","description":"在NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 機架系統案例中比較Grace與Blackwell記憶與72GPU NVLink域，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate grace/blackwell memory and 72-gpu nvlink domain within the NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 rack system case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：架構分析","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"針對Grace與Blackwell記憶提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for grace/blackwell memory.","instruction":"在「NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 機架系統」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識Grace與Blackwell記憶。CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 建立節點與記憶體層級的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是Grace–Blackwell、機架 NVLink 與液冷。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify grace/blackwell memory in the mentor diagram and primary sources for NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 rack system. CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of nodes and memory hierarchy, focusing on grace-blackwell, rack nvlink and liquid cooling. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交Grace與Blackwell記憶的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for grace/blackwell memory.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-01-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：Grace與Blackwell記憶","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: Grace/Blackwell memory","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-01-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-01-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.025，使用 16 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=11.6364。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.025 and 16 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=11.6364. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就Grace與Blackwell記憶的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in grace/blackwell memory?","options":["CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。","統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.","Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：證據驗證","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-01"],"objective":"針對Grace與Blackwell記憶提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for grace/blackwell memory.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點與記憶體層級」模型，檢查Grace與Blackwell記憶的兩個假想案例。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous nodes and memory hierarchy model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving grace/blackwell memory. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交Grace與Blackwell記憶的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for grace/blackwell memory.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-02-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：Grace與Blackwell記憶","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: Grace/Blackwell memory","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-02-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-02-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.025，使用 16 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=11.6364。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.025 and 16 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=11.6364. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就Grace與Blackwell記憶的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in grace/blackwell memory?","options":["統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：架構分析","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-02"],"objective":"針對72GPU NVLink域提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for 72-gpu nvlink domain.","instruction":"在「NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 機架系統」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識72GPU NVLink域。高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 建立節點內與節點間網路的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是Grace–Blackwell、機架 NVLink 與液冷。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify 72-gpu nvlink domain in the mentor diagram and primary sources for NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 rack system. Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of intranode and internode networks, focusing on grace-blackwell, rack nvlink and liquid cooling. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交72GPU NVLink域的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for 72-gpu nvlink domain.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-03-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：72GPU NVLink域","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: 72-GPU NVLink domain","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-03-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就72GPU NVLink域的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in 72-gpu nvlink domain?","options":["節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。"],"optionsEn":["Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：證據驗證","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-03"],"objective":"針對72GPU NVLink域提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for 72-gpu nvlink domain.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點內與節點間網路」模型，檢查72GPU NVLink域的兩個假想案例。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous intranode and internode networks model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving 72-gpu nvlink domain. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交72GPU NVLink域的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for 72-gpu nvlink domain.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-04-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：72GPU NVLink域","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: 72-GPU NVLink domain","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-04-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就72GPU NVLink域的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in 72-gpu nvlink domain?","options":["按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}}]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-stage2","order":2,"title":"功能架構與量化模型","titleEn":"Functional architecture and quantitative models","description":"在NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 機架系統案例中比較機架模型分割與存儲與checkpoint，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate rack-scale model partition and storage and checkpoints within the NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 rack system case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：架構分析","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-04"],"objective":"針對機架模型分割提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for rack-scale model partition.","instruction":"在「NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 機架系統」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識機架模型分割。串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 建立工作分割與平行效率的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是Grace–Blackwell、機架 NVLink 與液冷。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify rack-scale model partition in the mentor diagram and primary sources for NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 rack system. Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of work partition and parallel efficiency, focusing on grace-blackwell, rack nvlink and liquid cooling. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交機架模型分割的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for rack-scale model partition.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-05-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：機架模型分割","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: Rack-scale model partition","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-05-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就機架模型分割的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in rack-scale model partition?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：證據驗證","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-05"],"objective":"針對機架模型分割提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for rack-scale model partition.","instruction":"沿用前一步「工作分割與平行效率」模型，檢查機架模型分割的兩個假想案例。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous work partition and parallel efficiency model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving rack-scale model partition. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交機架模型分割的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for rack-scale model partition.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-06-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：機架模型分割","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: Rack-scale model partition","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-06-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就機架模型分割的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in rack-scale model partition?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."],"answer":2,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：架構分析","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-06"],"objective":"針對存儲與checkpoint提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for storage and checkpoints.","instruction":"在「NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 機架系統」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識存儲與checkpoint。暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 建立儲存階層與檢查點的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是Grace–Blackwell、機架 NVLink 與液冷。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify storage and checkpoints in the mentor diagram and primary sources for NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 rack system. Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of storage tiers and checkpoints, focusing on grace-blackwell, rack nvlink and liquid cooling. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交存儲與checkpoint的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for storage and checkpoints.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-07-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：存儲與checkpoint","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: Storage and checkpoints","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-07-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就存儲與checkpoint的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in storage and checkpoints?","options":["暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。","容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.","Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：證據驗證","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-07"],"objective":"針對存儲與checkpoint提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for storage and checkpoints.","instruction":"沿用前一步「儲存階層與檢查點」模型，檢查存儲與checkpoint的兩個假想案例。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous storage tiers and checkpoints model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving storage and checkpoints. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交存儲與checkpoint的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for storage and checkpoints.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-08-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：存儲與checkpoint","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: Storage and checkpoints","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-08-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就存儲與checkpoint的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in storage and checkpoints?","options":["容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}}]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-stage3","order":3,"title":"獨立驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Independent validation and engineering handoff","description":"在NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 機架系統案例中比較液冷與機架供電與服務邊界與復原，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate liquid cooling and rack power and service boundaries and recovery within the NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 rack system case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：架構分析","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-08"],"objective":"針對液冷與機架供電提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for liquid cooling and rack power.","instruction":"在「NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 機架系統」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識液冷與機架供電。設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 建立供電冷卻與設施的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是Grace–Blackwell、機架 NVLink 與液冷。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify liquid cooling and rack power in the mentor diagram and primary sources for NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 rack system. Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of power, cooling and facilities, focusing on grace-blackwell, rack nvlink and liquid cooling. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交液冷與機架供電的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for liquid cooling and rack power.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-09-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：液冷與機架供電","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: Liquid cooling and rack power","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-09-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就液冷與機架供電的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in liquid cooling and rack power?","options":["低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。"],"optionsEn":["Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：證據驗證","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-09"],"objective":"針對液冷與機架供電提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for liquid cooling and rack power.","instruction":"沿用前一步「供電冷卻與設施」模型，檢查液冷與機架供電的兩個假想案例。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous power, cooling and facilities model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving liquid cooling and rack power. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交液冷與機架供電的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for liquid cooling and rack power.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-10-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：液冷與機架供電","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: Liquid cooling and rack power","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-10-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就液冷與機架供電的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in liquid cooling and rack power?","options":["覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"title":"排程隔離與復原：架構分析","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-10"],"objective":"針對服務邊界與復原提出可反駁的排程隔離與復原模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable scheduling, isolation and recovery model and evidence record for service boundaries and recovery.","instruction":"在「NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 機架系統」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識服務邊界與復原。多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 建立排程隔離與復原的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是Grace–Blackwell、機架 NVLink 與液冷。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify service boundaries and recovery in the mentor diagram and primary sources for NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 rack system. Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of scheduling, isolation and recovery, focusing on grace-blackwell, rack nvlink and liquid cooling. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","observationEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table.","failure":"常見誤判：換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","check":"提交服務邊界與復原的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for service boundaries and recovery.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-11-k1","title":"排程隔離與復原","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery","text":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 本課架構對應：服務邊界與復原","textEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Course architecture correspondence: Service boundaries and recovery","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-11-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-11-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.025，使用 16 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=11.6364。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.025 and 16 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=11.6364. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就服務邊界與復原的「排程隔離與復原」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for scheduling, isolation and recovery in service boundaries and recovery?","options":["換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","explanationEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."}},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"title":"排程隔離與復原：證據驗證","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-11"],"objective":"針對服務邊界與復原提出可反駁的排程隔離與復原模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable scheduling, isolation and recovery model and evidence record for service boundaries and recovery.","instruction":"沿用前一步「排程隔離與復原」模型，檢查服務邊界與復原的兩個假想案例。在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous scheduling, isolation and recovery model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving service boundaries and recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","observationEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table.","failure":"常見誤判：換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","check":"提交服務邊界與復原的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for service boundaries and recovery.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-12-k1","title":"排程隔離與復原","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery","text":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 本課架構對應：服務邊界與復原","textEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Course architecture correspondence: Service boundaries and recovery","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-12-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"]},{"id":"v11-gb200-nvl72-v11-12-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.025，使用 16 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=11.6364。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.025 and 16 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=11.6364. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200","v11x-blackwell"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就服務邊界與復原的「排程隔離與復原」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for scheduling, isolation and recovery in service boundaries and recovery?","options":["換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","explanationEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."}}]}],"summary":"以Grace–Blackwell、機架 NVLink 與液冷解析NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 機架系統：六個原理與架構單元、十二項可保存的分析及驗證作業，附假想量化例、來源及衍生工程比較。","summaryEn":"Explore NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 rack system through grace-blackwell, rack nvlink and liquid cooling: six principle/architecture units and twelve saved analysis/validation tasks, with an assumed numerical example, primary sources and related engineering comparisons.","scope":"公開伺服器與超算架構的離線工作流、通信、儲存及能量模型；非機櫃接線、供電施工或實體維護SOP，也不表示學員取得廠商／研究中心設備存取。","scopeEn":"Offline workflow, fabric, storage and energy models of public servers/HPC. No rack-wiring, power-installation or physical-maintenance SOP and no vendor/research-center hardware access is implied.","workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.025，使用 16 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=11.6364。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.025 and 16 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=11.6364. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變模型邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are independently selected assumptions, not measured hardware, ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after boundary changes.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開架構及領域原理，不宣稱來源提供這組假想數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public architecture and principles, not these assumed measurements."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["Grace與Blackwell記憶","72GPU NVLink域","機架模型分割","存儲與checkpoint","液冷與機架供電","服務邊界與復原"],"labelsEn":["Grace/Blackwell memory","72-GPU NVLink domain","Rack-scale model partition","Storage and checkpoints","Liquid cooling and rack power","Service boundaries and recovery"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"vendorHints":[{"name":"NVIDIA","nameEn":"NVIDIA","url":"https://docs.nvidia.com/multi-node-nvlink-systems/multi-node-tuning-guide/overview.html","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-gb200"]},{"name":"NVIDIA","nameEn":"NVIDIA","url":"https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/blackwell-ai-computing-platform","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-blackwell"]}],"architectureNodes":[["計算節點","Compute nodes"],["本地記憶體","Local memory"],["叢集網路","Cluster fabric"],["儲存階層","Storage tiers"],["供電與冷卻","Power and cooling"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[0,2],[2,3],[4,0]],"architectureFamily":"server","educationEdition":11,"enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"v11-el-capitan","title":"El Capitan MI300A 超級電腦","titleEn":"El Capitan MI300A supercomputer","category":"computing","subcategory":"servers-hpc","subcategoryTitle":"大型計算系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Large computing systems","learningTrack":"servers","learningSubdiscipline":"servers-hpc","learningTags":["servers","servers-hpc","el-capitan"],"kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"curriculumVersion":11,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":420,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"stages":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-stage1","order":1,"title":"系統邊界與基本原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and principles","description":"在El Capitan MI300A 超級電腦案例中比較MI300A共享HBM與APU與Slingshot網絡，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate mi300a shared hbm and apu and slingshot fabrics within the El Capitan MI300A supercomputer case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：架構分析","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"針對MI300A共享HBM提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for mi300a shared hbm.","instruction":"在「El Capitan MI300A 超級電腦」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識MI300A共享HBM。CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 建立節點與記憶體層級的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是APU 共享 HBM 與 Slingshot 系統架構。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify mi300a shared hbm in the mentor diagram and primary sources for El Capitan MI300A supercomputer. CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of nodes and memory hierarchy, focusing on apu shared hbm and slingshot systems. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交MI300A共享HBM的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for mi300a shared hbm.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-01-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：MI300A共享HBM","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: MI300A shared HBM","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-01-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-01-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.030，使用 24 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=14.2012。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.030 and 24 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=14.2012. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就MI300A共享HBM的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in mi300a shared hbm?","options":["CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。","統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.","Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：證據驗證","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-el-capitan-v11-01"],"objective":"針對MI300A共享HBM提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for mi300a shared hbm.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點與記憶體層級」模型，檢查MI300A共享HBM的兩個假想案例。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous nodes and memory hierarchy model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving mi300a shared hbm. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交MI300A共享HBM的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for mi300a shared hbm.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-02-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：MI300A共享HBM","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: MI300A shared HBM","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-02-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-02-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.030，使用 24 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=14.2012。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.030 and 24 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=14.2012. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就MI300A共享HBM的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in mi300a shared hbm?","options":["統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：架構分析","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-el-capitan-v11-02"],"objective":"針對APU與Slingshot網絡提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for apu and slingshot fabrics.","instruction":"在「El Capitan MI300A 超級電腦」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識APU與Slingshot網絡。高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 建立節點內與節點間網路的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是APU 共享 HBM 與 Slingshot 系統架構。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify apu and slingshot fabrics in the mentor diagram and primary sources for El Capitan MI300A supercomputer. Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of intranode and internode networks, focusing on apu shared hbm and slingshot systems. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交APU與Slingshot網絡的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for apu and slingshot fabrics.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-03-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：APU與Slingshot網絡","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: APU and Slingshot fabrics","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-03-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就APU與Slingshot網絡的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in apu and slingshot fabrics?","options":["節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。"],"optionsEn":["Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：證據驗證","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-el-capitan-v11-03"],"objective":"針對APU與Slingshot網絡提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for apu and slingshot fabrics.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點內與節點間網路」模型，檢查APU與Slingshot網絡的兩個假想案例。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous intranode and internode networks model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving apu and slingshot fabrics. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交APU與Slingshot網絡的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for apu and slingshot fabrics.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-04-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：APU與Slingshot網絡","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: APU and Slingshot fabrics","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-04-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就APU與Slingshot網絡的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in apu and slingshot fabrics?","options":["按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}}]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-stage2","order":2,"title":"功能架構與量化模型","titleEn":"Functional architecture and quantitative models","description":"在El Capitan MI300A 超級電腦案例中比較NUMA工作分佈與Lustre與近端存儲，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate numa work distribution and lustre and near-node storage within the El Capitan MI300A supercomputer case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：架構分析","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-el-capitan-v11-04"],"objective":"針對NUMA工作分佈提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for numa work distribution.","instruction":"在「El Capitan MI300A 超級電腦」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識NUMA工作分佈。串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 建立工作分割與平行效率的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是APU 共享 HBM 與 Slingshot 系統架構。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify numa work distribution in the mentor diagram and primary sources for El Capitan MI300A supercomputer. Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of work partition and parallel efficiency, focusing on apu shared hbm and slingshot systems. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交NUMA工作分佈的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for numa work distribution.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-05-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：NUMA工作分佈","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: NUMA work distribution","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-05-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就NUMA工作分佈的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in numa work distribution?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：證據驗證","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-el-capitan-v11-05"],"objective":"針對NUMA工作分佈提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for numa work distribution.","instruction":"沿用前一步「工作分割與平行效率」模型，檢查NUMA工作分佈的兩個假想案例。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous work partition and parallel efficiency model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving numa work distribution. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交NUMA工作分佈的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for numa work distribution.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-06-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：NUMA工作分佈","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: NUMA work distribution","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-06-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就NUMA工作分佈的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in numa work distribution?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."],"answer":2,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：架構分析","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-el-capitan-v11-06"],"objective":"針對Lustre與近端存儲提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for lustre and near-node storage.","instruction":"在「El Capitan MI300A 超級電腦」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識Lustre與近端存儲。暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 建立儲存階層與檢查點的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是APU 共享 HBM 與 Slingshot 系統架構。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify lustre and near-node storage in the mentor diagram and primary sources for El Capitan MI300A supercomputer. Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of storage tiers and checkpoints, focusing on apu shared hbm and slingshot systems. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交Lustre與近端存儲的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for lustre and near-node storage.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-07-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：Lustre與近端存儲","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: Lustre and near-node storage","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-07-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就Lustre與近端存儲的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in lustre and near-node storage?","options":["暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。","容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.","Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：證據驗證","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-el-capitan-v11-07"],"objective":"針對Lustre與近端存儲提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for lustre and near-node storage.","instruction":"沿用前一步「儲存階層與檢查點」模型，檢查Lustre與近端存儲的兩個假想案例。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous storage tiers and checkpoints model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving lustre and near-node storage. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交Lustre與近端存儲的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for lustre and near-node storage.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-08-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：Lustre與近端存儲","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: Lustre and near-node storage","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-08-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就Lustre與近端存儲的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in lustre and near-node storage?","options":["容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}}]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-stage3","order":3,"title":"獨立驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Independent validation and engineering handoff","description":"在El Capitan MI300A 超級電腦案例中比較液冷與設施功率與節點排程與一致性，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate liquid cooling and facility power and node scheduling and consistency within the El Capitan MI300A supercomputer case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：架構分析","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-el-capitan-v11-08"],"objective":"針對液冷與設施功率提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for liquid cooling and facility power.","instruction":"在「El Capitan MI300A 超級電腦」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識液冷與設施功率。設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 建立供電冷卻與設施的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是APU 共享 HBM 與 Slingshot 系統架構。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify liquid cooling and facility power in the mentor diagram and primary sources for El Capitan MI300A supercomputer. Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of power, cooling and facilities, focusing on apu shared hbm and slingshot systems. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交液冷與設施功率的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for liquid cooling and facility power.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-09-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：液冷與設施功率","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: Liquid cooling and facility power","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-09-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就液冷與設施功率的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in liquid cooling and facility power?","options":["低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。"],"optionsEn":["Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：證據驗證","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-el-capitan-v11-09"],"objective":"針對液冷與設施功率提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for liquid cooling and facility power.","instruction":"沿用前一步「供電冷卻與設施」模型，檢查液冷與設施功率的兩個假想案例。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous power, cooling and facilities model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving liquid cooling and facility power. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交液冷與設施功率的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for liquid cooling and facility power.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-10-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：液冷與設施功率","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: Liquid cooling and facility power","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-10-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就液冷與設施功率的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in liquid cooling and facility power?","options":["覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"title":"排程隔離與復原：架構分析","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-el-capitan-v11-10"],"objective":"針對節點排程與一致性提出可反駁的排程隔離與復原模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable scheduling, isolation and recovery model and evidence record for node scheduling and consistency.","instruction":"在「El Capitan MI300A 超級電腦」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識節點排程與一致性。多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 建立排程隔離與復原的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是APU 共享 HBM 與 Slingshot 系統架構。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify node scheduling and consistency in the mentor diagram and primary sources for El Capitan MI300A supercomputer. Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of scheduling, isolation and recovery, focusing on apu shared hbm and slingshot systems. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","observationEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table.","failure":"常見誤判：換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","check":"提交節點排程與一致性的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for node scheduling and consistency.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-11-k1","title":"排程隔離與復原","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery","text":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 本課架構對應：節點排程與一致性","textEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Course architecture correspondence: Node scheduling and consistency","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-11-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-11-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.030，使用 24 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=14.2012。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.030 and 24 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=14.2012. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就節點排程與一致性的「排程隔離與復原」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for scheduling, isolation and recovery in node scheduling and consistency?","options":["換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","explanationEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."}},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"title":"排程隔離與復原：證據驗證","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-el-capitan-v11-11"],"objective":"針對節點排程與一致性提出可反駁的排程隔離與復原模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable scheduling, isolation and recovery model and evidence record for node scheduling and consistency.","instruction":"沿用前一步「排程隔離與復原」模型，檢查節點排程與一致性的兩個假想案例。在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous scheduling, isolation and recovery model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving node scheduling and consistency. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","observationEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table.","failure":"常見誤判：換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","check":"提交節點排程與一致性的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for node scheduling and consistency.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-12-k1","title":"排程隔離與復原","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery","text":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 本課架構對應：節點排程與一致性","textEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Course architecture correspondence: Node scheduling and consistency","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-12-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-el-capitan-v11-12-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.030，使用 24 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=14.2012。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.030 and 24 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=14.2012. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan","v11x-perlmutter"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就節點排程與一致性的「排程隔離與復原」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for scheduling, isolation and recovery in node scheduling and consistency?","options":["換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","explanationEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."}}]}],"summary":"以APU 共享 HBM 與 Slingshot 系統架構解析El Capitan MI300A 超級電腦：六個原理與架構單元、十二項可保存的分析及驗證作業，附假想量化例、來源及衍生工程比較。","summaryEn":"Explore El Capitan MI300A supercomputer through apu shared hbm and slingshot systems: six principle/architecture units and twelve saved analysis/validation tasks, with an assumed numerical example, primary sources and related engineering comparisons.","scope":"公開伺服器與超算架構的離線工作流、通信、儲存及能量模型；非機櫃接線、供電施工或實體維護SOP，也不表示學員取得廠商／研究中心設備存取。","scopeEn":"Offline workflow, fabric, storage and energy models of public servers/HPC. No rack-wiring, power-installation or physical-maintenance SOP and no vendor/research-center hardware access is implied.","workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.030，使用 24 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=14.2012。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.030 and 24 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=14.2012. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變模型邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are independently selected assumptions, not measured hardware, ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after boundary changes.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開架構及領域原理，不宣稱來源提供這組假想數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public architecture and principles, not these assumed measurements."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["MI300A共享HBM","APU與Slingshot網絡","NUMA工作分佈","Lustre與近端存儲","液冷與設施功率","節點排程與一致性"],"labelsEn":["MI300A shared HBM","APU and Slingshot fabrics","NUMA work distribution","Lustre and near-node storage","Liquid cooling and facility power","Node scheduling and consistency"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"vendorHints":[{"name":"Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory","nameEn":"Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory","url":"https://hpc.llnl.gov/documentation/user-guides/using-el-capitan-systems/hardware-overview","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-elcapitan"]},{"name":"NERSC","nameEn":"NERSC","url":"https://docs.nersc.gov/systems/perlmutter/architecture/","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter"]}],"architectureNodes":[["計算節點","Compute nodes"],["本地記憶體","Local memory"],["叢集網路","Cluster fabric"],["儲存階層","Storage tiers"],["供電與冷卻","Power and cooling"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[0,2],[2,3],[4,0]],"architectureFamily":"server","educationEdition":11,"enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"v11-alps","title":"Alps Grace–Hopper 超級電腦","titleEn":"Alps Grace-Hopper supercomputer","category":"computing","subcategory":"servers-hpc","subcategoryTitle":"大型計算系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Large computing systems","learningTrack":"servers","learningSubdiscipline":"servers-hpc","learningTags":["servers","servers-hpc","alps"],"kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"curriculumVersion":11,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":420,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"stages":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-stage1","order":1,"title":"系統邊界與基本原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and principles","description":"在Alps Grace–Hopper 超級電腦案例中比較GH200相干記憶與node內與Slingshot，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate gh200 coherent memory and intranode and slingshot within the Alps Grace-Hopper supercomputer case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：架構分析","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"針對GH200相干記憶提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for gh200 coherent memory.","instruction":"在「Alps Grace–Hopper 超級電腦」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識GH200相干記憶。CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 建立節點與記憶體層級的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是異質節點分區及 CPU–GPU 相干互連。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify gh200 coherent memory in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Alps Grace-Hopper supercomputer. CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of nodes and memory hierarchy, focusing on heterogeneous partitions and coherent cpu-gpu links. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交GH200相干記憶的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for gh200 coherent memory.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-01-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：GH200相干記憶","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: GH200 coherent memory","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-01-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-01-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.035，使用 32 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=15.3477。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.035 and 32 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=15.3477. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就GH200相干記憶的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in gh200 coherent memory?","options":["CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。","統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.","Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：證據驗證","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-alps-v11-01"],"objective":"針對GH200相干記憶提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for gh200 coherent memory.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點與記憶體層級」模型，檢查GH200相干記憶的兩個假想案例。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous nodes and memory hierarchy model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving gh200 coherent memory. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交GH200相干記憶的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for gh200 coherent memory.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-02-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：GH200相干記憶","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: GH200 coherent memory","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-02-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-02-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.035，使用 32 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=15.3477。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.035 and 32 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=15.3477. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就GH200相干記憶的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in gh200 coherent memory?","options":["統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：架構分析","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-alps-v11-02"],"objective":"針對node內與Slingshot提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for intranode and slingshot.","instruction":"在「Alps Grace–Hopper 超級電腦」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識node內與Slingshot。高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 建立節點內與節點間網路的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是異質節點分區及 CPU–GPU 相干互連。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify intranode and slingshot in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Alps Grace-Hopper supercomputer. Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of intranode and internode networks, focusing on heterogeneous partitions and coherent cpu-gpu links. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交node內與Slingshot的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for intranode and slingshot.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-03-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：node內與Slingshot","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: Intranode and Slingshot","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-03-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就node內與Slingshot的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in intranode and slingshot?","options":["節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。"],"optionsEn":["Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：證據驗證","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-alps-v11-03"],"objective":"針對node內與Slingshot提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for intranode and slingshot.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點內與節點間網路」模型，檢查node內與Slingshot的兩個假想案例。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous intranode and internode networks model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving intranode and slingshot. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交node內與Slingshot的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for intranode and slingshot.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-04-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：node內與Slingshot","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: Intranode and Slingshot","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-04-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就node內與Slingshot的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in intranode and slingshot?","options":["按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}}]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-stage2","order":2,"title":"功能架構與量化模型","titleEn":"Functional architecture and quantitative models","description":"在Alps Grace–Hopper 超級電腦案例中比較異質partition選擇與scratch與archive，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate heterogeneous partition choice and scratch and archive within the Alps Grace-Hopper supercomputer case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：架構分析","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-alps-v11-04"],"objective":"針對異質partition選擇提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for heterogeneous partition choice.","instruction":"在「Alps Grace–Hopper 超級電腦」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識異質partition選擇。串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 建立工作分割與平行效率的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是異質節點分區及 CPU–GPU 相干互連。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify heterogeneous partition choice in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Alps Grace-Hopper supercomputer. Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of work partition and parallel efficiency, focusing on heterogeneous partitions and coherent cpu-gpu links. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交異質partition選擇的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for heterogeneous partition choice.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-05-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：異質partition選擇","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: Heterogeneous partition choice","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-05-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就異質partition選擇的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in heterogeneous partition choice?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：證據驗證","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-alps-v11-05"],"objective":"針對異質partition選擇提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for heterogeneous partition choice.","instruction":"沿用前一步「工作分割與平行效率」模型，檢查異質partition選擇的兩個假想案例。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous work partition and parallel efficiency model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving heterogeneous partition choice. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交異質partition選擇的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for heterogeneous partition choice.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-06-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：異質partition選擇","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: Heterogeneous partition choice","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-06-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就異質partition選擇的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in heterogeneous partition choice?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."],"answer":2,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：架構分析","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-alps-v11-06"],"objective":"針對scratch與archive提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for scratch and archive.","instruction":"在「Alps Grace–Hopper 超級電腦」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識scratch與archive。暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 建立儲存階層與檢查點的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是異質節點分區及 CPU–GPU 相干互連。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify scratch and archive in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Alps Grace-Hopper supercomputer. Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of storage tiers and checkpoints, focusing on heterogeneous partitions and coherent cpu-gpu links. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交scratch與archive的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for scratch and archive.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-07-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：scratch與archive","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: Scratch and archive","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-07-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就scratch與archive的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in scratch and archive?","options":["暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。","容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.","Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：證據驗證","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-alps-v11-07"],"objective":"針對scratch與archive提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for scratch and archive.","instruction":"沿用前一步「儲存階層與檢查點」模型，檢查scratch與archive的兩個假想案例。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous storage tiers and checkpoints model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving scratch and archive. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交scratch與archive的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for scratch and archive.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-08-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：scratch與archive","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: Scratch and archive","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-08-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就scratch與archive的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in scratch and archive?","options":["容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}}]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-stage3","order":3,"title":"獨立驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Independent validation and engineering handoff","description":"在Alps Grace–Hopper 超級電腦案例中比較機櫃冷卻預算與分區作業復原，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate cabinet cooling budget and partition job recovery within the Alps Grace-Hopper supercomputer case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：架構分析","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-alps-v11-08"],"objective":"針對機櫃冷卻預算提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for cabinet cooling budget.","instruction":"在「Alps Grace–Hopper 超級電腦」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識機櫃冷卻預算。設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 建立供電冷卻與設施的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是異質節點分區及 CPU–GPU 相干互連。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify cabinet cooling budget in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Alps Grace-Hopper supercomputer. Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of power, cooling and facilities, focusing on heterogeneous partitions and coherent cpu-gpu links. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交機櫃冷卻預算的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for cabinet cooling budget.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-09-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：機櫃冷卻預算","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: Cabinet cooling budget","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-09-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就機櫃冷卻預算的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in cabinet cooling budget?","options":["低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。"],"optionsEn":["Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：證據驗證","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-alps-v11-09"],"objective":"針對機櫃冷卻預算提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for cabinet cooling budget.","instruction":"沿用前一步「供電冷卻與設施」模型，檢查機櫃冷卻預算的兩個假想案例。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous power, cooling and facilities model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving cabinet cooling budget. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交機櫃冷卻預算的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for cabinet cooling budget.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-10-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：機櫃冷卻預算","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: Cabinet cooling budget","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-10-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就機櫃冷卻預算的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in cabinet cooling budget?","options":["覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"title":"排程隔離與復原：架構分析","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-alps-v11-10"],"objective":"針對分區作業復原提出可反駁的排程隔離與復原模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable scheduling, isolation and recovery model and evidence record for partition job recovery.","instruction":"在「Alps Grace–Hopper 超級電腦」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識分區作業復原。多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 建立排程隔離與復原的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是異質節點分區及 CPU–GPU 相干互連。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify partition job recovery in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Alps Grace-Hopper supercomputer. Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of scheduling, isolation and recovery, focusing on heterogeneous partitions and coherent cpu-gpu links. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","observationEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table.","failure":"常見誤判：換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","check":"提交分區作業復原的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for partition job recovery.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-11-k1","title":"排程隔離與復原","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery","text":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 本課架構對應：分區作業復原","textEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Course architecture correspondence: Partition job recovery","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-11-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-11-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.035，使用 32 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=15.3477。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.035 and 32 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=15.3477. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就分區作業復原的「排程隔離與復原」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for scheduling, isolation and recovery in partition job recovery?","options":["換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","explanationEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."}},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"title":"排程隔離與復原：證據驗證","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-alps-v11-11"],"objective":"針對分區作業復原提出可反駁的排程隔離與復原模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable scheduling, isolation and recovery model and evidence record for partition job recovery.","instruction":"沿用前一步「排程隔離與復原」模型，檢查分區作業復原的兩個假想案例。在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous scheduling, isolation and recovery model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving partition job recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","observationEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table.","failure":"常見誤判：換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","check":"提交分區作業復原的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for partition job recovery.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-alps-v11-12-k1","title":"排程隔離與復原","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery","text":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 本課架構對應：分區作業復原","textEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Course architecture correspondence: Partition job recovery","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-12-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-alps-v11-12-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.035，使用 32 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=15.3477。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.035 and 32 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=15.3477. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps","v11x-perlmutter"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就分區作業復原的「排程隔離與復原」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for scheduling, isolation and recovery in partition job recovery?","options":["換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","explanationEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."}}]}],"summary":"以異質節點分區及 CPU–GPU 相干互連解析Alps Grace–Hopper 超級電腦：六個原理與架構單元、十二項可保存的分析及驗證作業，附假想量化例、來源及衍生工程比較。","summaryEn":"Explore Alps Grace-Hopper supercomputer through heterogeneous partitions and coherent cpu-gpu links: six principle/architecture units and twelve saved analysis/validation tasks, with an assumed numerical example, primary sources and related engineering comparisons.","scope":"公開伺服器與超算架構的離線工作流、通信、儲存及能量模型；非機櫃接線、供電施工或實體維護SOP，也不表示學員取得廠商／研究中心設備存取。","scopeEn":"Offline workflow, fabric, storage and energy models of public servers/HPC. No rack-wiring, power-installation or physical-maintenance SOP and no vendor/research-center hardware access is implied.","workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.035，使用 32 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=15.3477。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.035 and 32 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=15.3477. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變模型邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are independently selected assumptions, not measured hardware, ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after boundary changes.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開架構及領域原理，不宣稱來源提供這組假想數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public architecture and principles, not these assumed measurements."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["GH200相干記憶","node內與Slingshot","異質partition選擇","scratch與archive","機櫃冷卻預算","分區作業復原"],"labelsEn":["GH200 coherent memory","Intranode and Slingshot","Heterogeneous partition choice","Scratch and archive","Cabinet cooling budget","Partition job recovery"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"vendorHints":[{"name":"CSCS","nameEn":"CSCS","url":"https://docs.cscs.ch/alps/hardware/","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-alps"]},{"name":"NERSC","nameEn":"NERSC","url":"https://docs.nersc.gov/systems/perlmutter/architecture/","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter"]}],"architectureNodes":[["計算節點","Compute nodes"],["本地記憶體","Local memory"],["叢集網路","Cluster fabric"],["儲存階層","Storage tiers"],["供電與冷卻","Power and cooling"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[0,2],[2,3],[4,0]],"architectureFamily":"server","educationEdition":11,"enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"v11-perlmutter","title":"Perlmutter GPU 與 CPU 雙分區","titleEn":"Perlmutter GPU and CPU partitions","category":"computing","subcategory":"servers-hpc","subcategoryTitle":"大型計算系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Large computing systems","learningTrack":"servers","learningSubdiscipline":"servers-hpc","learningTags":["servers","servers-hpc","perlmutter"],"kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"curriculumVersion":11,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":420,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"stages":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-stage1","order":1,"title":"系統邊界與基本原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and principles","description":"在Perlmutter GPU 與 CPU 雙分區案例中比較A100與EPYC拓撲與Dragonfly光銅連線，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate a100/epyc topology and dragonfly optical/copper links within the Perlmutter GPU and CPU partitions case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：架構分析","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"針對A100與EPYC拓撲提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for a100/epyc topology.","instruction":"在「Perlmutter GPU 與 CPU 雙分區」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識A100與EPYC拓撲。CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 建立節點與記憶體層級的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是雙分區、Dragonfly 網路與全快閃暫存。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify a100/epyc topology in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Perlmutter GPU and CPU partitions. CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of nodes and memory hierarchy, focusing on dual partitions, dragonfly and all-flash scratch. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交A100與EPYC拓撲的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for a100/epyc topology.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-01-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：A100與EPYC拓撲","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: A100/EPYC topology","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-01-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-01-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.020，使用 8 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=7.0175。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.020 and 8 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=7.0175. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就A100與EPYC拓撲的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in a100/epyc topology?","options":["CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。","統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.","Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：證據驗證","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-perlmutter-v11-01"],"objective":"針對A100與EPYC拓撲提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for a100/epyc topology.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點與記憶體層級」模型，檢查A100與EPYC拓撲的兩個假想案例。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous nodes and memory hierarchy model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving a100/epyc topology. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交A100與EPYC拓撲的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for a100/epyc topology.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-02-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：A100與EPYC拓撲","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: A100/EPYC topology","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-02-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-02-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.020，使用 8 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=7.0175。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.020 and 8 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=7.0175. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就A100與EPYC拓撲的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in a100/epyc topology?","options":["統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：架構分析","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-perlmutter-v11-02"],"objective":"針對Dragonfly光銅連線提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for dragonfly optical/copper links.","instruction":"在「Perlmutter GPU 與 CPU 雙分區」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識Dragonfly光銅連線。高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 建立節點內與節點間網路的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是雙分區、Dragonfly 網路與全快閃暫存。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify dragonfly optical/copper links in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Perlmutter GPU and CPU partitions. Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of intranode and internode networks, focusing on dual partitions, dragonfly and all-flash scratch. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交Dragonfly光銅連線的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for dragonfly optical/copper links.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-03-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：Dragonfly光銅連線","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: Dragonfly optical/copper links","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-03-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就Dragonfly光銅連線的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in dragonfly optical/copper links?","options":["節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。"],"optionsEn":["Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：證據驗證","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-perlmutter-v11-03"],"objective":"針對Dragonfly光銅連線提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for dragonfly optical/copper links.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點內與節點間網路」模型，檢查Dragonfly光銅連線的兩個假想案例。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous intranode and internode networks model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving dragonfly optical/copper links. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交Dragonfly光銅連線的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for dragonfly optical/copper links.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-04-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：Dragonfly光銅連線","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: Dragonfly optical/copper links","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-04-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就Dragonfly光銅連線的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in dragonfly optical/copper links?","options":["按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}}]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-stage2","order":2,"title":"功能架構與量化模型","titleEn":"Functional architecture and quantitative models","description":"在Perlmutter GPU 與 CPU 雙分區案例中比較CPU/GPU分工與all-flash與metadata，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate cpu/gpu partitioning and all-flash and metadata within the Perlmutter GPU and CPU partitions case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：架構分析","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-perlmutter-v11-04"],"objective":"針對CPU/GPU分工提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for cpu/gpu partitioning.","instruction":"在「Perlmutter GPU 與 CPU 雙分區」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識CPU/GPU分工。串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 建立工作分割與平行效率的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是雙分區、Dragonfly 網路與全快閃暫存。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify cpu/gpu partitioning in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Perlmutter GPU and CPU partitions. Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of work partition and parallel efficiency, focusing on dual partitions, dragonfly and all-flash scratch. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交CPU/GPU分工的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for cpu/gpu partitioning.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-05-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：CPU/GPU分工","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: CPU/GPU partitioning","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-05-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就CPU/GPU分工的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in cpu/gpu partitioning?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：證據驗證","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-perlmutter-v11-05"],"objective":"針對CPU/GPU分工提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for cpu/gpu partitioning.","instruction":"沿用前一步「工作分割與平行效率」模型，檢查CPU/GPU分工的兩個假想案例。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous work partition and parallel efficiency model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving cpu/gpu partitioning. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交CPU/GPU分工的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for cpu/gpu partitioning.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-06-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：CPU/GPU分工","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: CPU/GPU partitioning","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-06-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就CPU/GPU分工的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in cpu/gpu partitioning?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."],"answer":2,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：架構分析","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-perlmutter-v11-06"],"objective":"針對all-flash與metadata提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for all-flash and metadata.","instruction":"在「Perlmutter GPU 與 CPU 雙分區」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識all-flash與metadata。暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 建立儲存階層與檢查點的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是雙分區、Dragonfly 網路與全快閃暫存。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify all-flash and metadata in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Perlmutter GPU and CPU partitions. Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of storage tiers and checkpoints, focusing on dual partitions, dragonfly and all-flash scratch. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交all-flash與metadata的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for all-flash and metadata.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-07-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：all-flash與metadata","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: All-flash and metadata","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-07-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就all-flash與metadata的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in all-flash and metadata?","options":["暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。","容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.","Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：證據驗證","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-perlmutter-v11-07"],"objective":"針對all-flash與metadata提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for all-flash and metadata.","instruction":"沿用前一步「儲存階層與檢查點」模型，檢查all-flash與metadata的兩個假想案例。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous storage tiers and checkpoints model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving all-flash and metadata. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交all-flash與metadata的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for all-flash and metadata.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-08-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：all-flash與metadata","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: All-flash and metadata","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-08-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就all-flash與metadata的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in all-flash and metadata?","options":["容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}}]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-stage3","order":3,"title":"獨立驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Independent validation and engineering handoff","description":"在Perlmutter GPU 與 CPU 雙分區案例中比較機櫃與節點能量與排程與檢查點重啟，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate cabinet/node energy and scheduling/checkpoint restart within the Perlmutter GPU and CPU partitions case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：架構分析","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-perlmutter-v11-08"],"objective":"針對機櫃與節點能量提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for cabinet/node energy.","instruction":"在「Perlmutter GPU 與 CPU 雙分區」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識機櫃與節點能量。設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 建立供電冷卻與設施的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是雙分區、Dragonfly 網路與全快閃暫存。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify cabinet/node energy in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Perlmutter GPU and CPU partitions. Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of power, cooling and facilities, focusing on dual partitions, dragonfly and all-flash scratch. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交機櫃與節點能量的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for cabinet/node energy.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-09-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：機櫃與節點能量","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: Cabinet/node energy","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-09-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就機櫃與節點能量的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in cabinet/node energy?","options":["低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。"],"optionsEn":["Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：證據驗證","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-perlmutter-v11-09"],"objective":"針對機櫃與節點能量提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for cabinet/node energy.","instruction":"沿用前一步「供電冷卻與設施」模型，檢查機櫃與節點能量的兩個假想案例。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous power, cooling and facilities model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving cabinet/node energy. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交機櫃與節點能量的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for cabinet/node energy.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-10-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：機櫃與節點能量","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: Cabinet/node energy","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-10-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就機櫃與節點能量的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in cabinet/node energy?","options":["覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"title":"排程隔離與復原：架構分析","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-perlmutter-v11-10"],"objective":"針對排程與檢查點重啟提出可反駁的排程隔離與復原模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable scheduling, isolation and recovery model and evidence record for scheduling/checkpoint restart.","instruction":"在「Perlmutter GPU 與 CPU 雙分區」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識排程與檢查點重啟。多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 建立排程隔離與復原的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是雙分區、Dragonfly 網路與全快閃暫存。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify scheduling/checkpoint restart in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Perlmutter GPU and CPU partitions. Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of scheduling, isolation and recovery, focusing on dual partitions, dragonfly and all-flash scratch. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","observationEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table.","failure":"常見誤判：換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","check":"提交排程與檢查點重啟的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for scheduling/checkpoint restart.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-11-k1","title":"排程隔離與復原","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery","text":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 本課架構對應：排程與檢查點重啟","textEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Course architecture correspondence: Scheduling/checkpoint restart","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-11-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-11-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.020，使用 8 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=7.0175。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.020 and 8 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=7.0175. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就排程與檢查點重啟的「排程隔離與復原」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for scheduling, isolation and recovery in scheduling/checkpoint restart?","options":["換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","explanationEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."}},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"title":"排程隔離與復原：證據驗證","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-perlmutter-v11-11"],"objective":"針對排程與檢查點重啟提出可反駁的排程隔離與復原模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable scheduling, isolation and recovery model and evidence record for scheduling/checkpoint restart.","instruction":"沿用前一步「排程隔離與復原」模型，檢查排程與檢查點重啟的兩個假想案例。在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous scheduling, isolation and recovery model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving scheduling/checkpoint restart. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","observationEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table.","failure":"常見誤判：換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","check":"提交排程與檢查點重啟的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for scheduling/checkpoint restart.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-12-k1","title":"排程隔離與復原","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery","text":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 本課架構對應：排程與檢查點重啟","textEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Course architecture correspondence: Scheduling/checkpoint restart","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-12-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"]},{"id":"v11-perlmutter-v11-12-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.020，使用 8 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=7.0175。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.020 and 8 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=7.0175. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter","v11x-cuda"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就排程與檢查點重啟的「排程隔離與復原」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for scheduling, isolation and recovery in scheduling/checkpoint restart?","options":["換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","explanationEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."}}]}],"summary":"以雙分區、Dragonfly 網路與全快閃暫存解析Perlmutter GPU 與 CPU 雙分區：六個原理與架構單元、十二項可保存的分析及驗證作業，附假想量化例、來源及衍生工程比較。","summaryEn":"Explore Perlmutter GPU and CPU partitions through dual partitions, dragonfly and all-flash scratch: six principle/architecture units and twelve saved analysis/validation tasks, with an assumed numerical example, primary sources and related engineering comparisons.","scope":"公開伺服器與超算架構的離線工作流、通信、儲存及能量模型；非機櫃接線、供電施工或實體維護SOP，也不表示學員取得廠商／研究中心設備存取。","scopeEn":"Offline workflow, fabric, storage and energy models of public servers/HPC. No rack-wiring, power-installation or physical-maintenance SOP and no vendor/research-center hardware access is implied.","workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.020，使用 8 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=7.0175。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.020 and 8 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=7.0175. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變模型邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are independently selected assumptions, not measured hardware, ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after boundary changes.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開架構及領域原理，不宣稱來源提供這組假想數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public architecture and principles, not these assumed measurements."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["A100與EPYC拓撲","Dragonfly光銅連線","CPU/GPU分工","all-flash與metadata","機櫃與節點能量","排程與檢查點重啟"],"labelsEn":["A100/EPYC topology","Dragonfly optical/copper links","CPU/GPU partitioning","All-flash and metadata","Cabinet/node energy","Scheduling/checkpoint restart"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"vendorHints":[{"name":"NERSC","nameEn":"NERSC","url":"https://docs.nersc.gov/systems/perlmutter/architecture/","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter"]},{"name":"NVIDIA","nameEn":"NVIDIA","url":"https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-c-programming-guide/","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-cuda"]}],"architectureNodes":[["計算節點","Compute nodes"],["本地記憶體","Local memory"],["叢集網路","Cluster fabric"],["儲存階層","Storage tiers"],["供電與冷卻","Power and cooling"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[0,2],[2,3],[4,0]],"architectureFamily":"server","educationEdition":11,"enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"v11-leonardo","title":"Leonardo Booster 與資料分區","titleEn":"Leonardo Booster and data-centric partitions","category":"computing","subcategory":"servers-hpc","subcategoryTitle":"大型計算系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Large computing systems","learningTrack":"servers","learningSubdiscipline":"servers-hpc","learningTags":["servers","servers-hpc","leonardo"],"kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"curriculumVersion":11,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":420,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"stages":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-stage1","order":1,"title":"系統邊界與基本原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and principles","description":"在Leonardo Booster 與資料分區案例中比較Booster GPU與主機與InfiniBand層級，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate booster gpu and host and infiniband hierarchy within the Leonardo Booster and data-centric partitions case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：架構分析","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"針對Booster GPU與主機提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for booster gpu and host.","instruction":"在「Leonardo Booster 與資料分區」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識Booster GPU與主機。CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 建立節點與記憶體層級的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是GPU Booster 與通用節點的工作流分工。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify booster gpu and host in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Leonardo Booster and data-centric partitions. CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of nodes and memory hierarchy, focusing on gpu booster and general-node workflow division. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交Booster GPU與主機的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for booster gpu and host.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-01-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：Booster GPU與主機","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: Booster GPU and host","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-01-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-01-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.025，使用 16 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=11.6364。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.025 and 16 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=11.6364. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就Booster GPU與主機的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in booster gpu and host?","options":["CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。","統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.","Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：證據驗證","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-leonardo-v11-01"],"objective":"針對Booster GPU與主機提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for booster gpu and host.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點與記憶體層級」模型，檢查Booster GPU與主機的兩個假想案例。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous nodes and memory hierarchy model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving booster gpu and host. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交Booster GPU與主機的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for booster gpu and host.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-02-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：Booster GPU與主機","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: Booster GPU and host","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-02-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-02-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.025，使用 16 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=11.6364。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.025 and 16 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=11.6364. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就Booster GPU與主機的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in booster gpu and host?","options":["統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：架構分析","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-leonardo-v11-02"],"objective":"針對InfiniBand層級提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for infiniband hierarchy.","instruction":"在「Leonardo Booster 與資料分區」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識InfiniBand層級。高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 建立節點內與節點間網路的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是GPU Booster 與通用節點的工作流分工。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify infiniband hierarchy in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Leonardo Booster and data-centric partitions. Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of intranode and internode networks, focusing on gpu booster and general-node workflow division. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交InfiniBand層級的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for infiniband hierarchy.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-03-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：InfiniBand層級","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: InfiniBand hierarchy","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-03-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就InfiniBand層級的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in infiniband hierarchy?","options":["節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。"],"optionsEn":["Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：證據驗證","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-leonardo-v11-03"],"objective":"針對InfiniBand層級提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for infiniband hierarchy.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點內與節點間網路」模型，檢查InfiniBand層級的兩個假想案例。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous intranode and internode networks model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving infiniband hierarchy. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交InfiniBand層級的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for infiniband hierarchy.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-04-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：InfiniBand層級","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: InfiniBand hierarchy","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-04-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就InfiniBand層級的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in infiniband hierarchy?","options":["按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}}]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-stage2","order":2,"title":"功能架構與量化模型","titleEn":"Functional architecture and quantitative models","description":"在Leonardo Booster 與資料分區案例中比較partition工作流與高效與容量存儲，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate partition workflows and fast/capacity storage within the Leonardo Booster and data-centric partitions case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：架構分析","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-leonardo-v11-04"],"objective":"針對partition工作流提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for partition workflows.","instruction":"在「Leonardo Booster 與資料分區」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識partition工作流。串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 建立工作分割與平行效率的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是GPU Booster 與通用節點的工作流分工。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify partition workflows in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Leonardo Booster and data-centric partitions. Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of work partition and parallel efficiency, focusing on gpu booster and general-node workflow division. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交partition工作流的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for partition workflows.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-05-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：partition工作流","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: Partition workflows","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-05-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就partition工作流的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in partition workflows?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：證據驗證","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-leonardo-v11-05"],"objective":"針對partition工作流提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for partition workflows.","instruction":"沿用前一步「工作分割與平行效率」模型，檢查partition工作流的兩個假想案例。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous work partition and parallel efficiency model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving partition workflows. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交partition工作流的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for partition workflows.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-06-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：partition工作流","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: Partition workflows","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-06-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就partition工作流的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in partition workflows?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."],"answer":2,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：架構分析","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-leonardo-v11-06"],"objective":"針對高效與容量存儲提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for fast/capacity storage.","instruction":"在「Leonardo Booster 與資料分區」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識高效與容量存儲。暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 建立儲存階層與檢查點的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是GPU Booster 與通用節點的工作流分工。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify fast/capacity storage in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Leonardo Booster and data-centric partitions. Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of storage tiers and checkpoints, focusing on gpu booster and general-node workflow division. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交高效與容量存儲的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for fast/capacity storage.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-07-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：高效與容量存儲","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: Fast/capacity storage","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-07-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就高效與容量存儲的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in fast/capacity storage?","options":["暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。","容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.","Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：證據驗證","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-leonardo-v11-07"],"objective":"針對高效與容量存儲提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for fast/capacity storage.","instruction":"沿用前一步「儲存階層與檢查點」模型，檢查高效與容量存儲的兩個假想案例。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous storage tiers and checkpoints model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving fast/capacity storage. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交高效與容量存儲的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for fast/capacity storage.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-08-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：高效與容量存儲","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: Fast/capacity storage","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-08-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就高效與容量存儲的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in fast/capacity storage?","options":["容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}}]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-stage3","order":3,"title":"獨立驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Independent validation and engineering handoff","description":"在Leonardo Booster 與資料分區案例中比較計算分區能耗與跨分區排程，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate compute-partition energy and cross-partition scheduling within the Leonardo Booster and data-centric partitions case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：架構分析","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-leonardo-v11-08"],"objective":"針對計算分區能耗提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for compute-partition energy.","instruction":"在「Leonardo Booster 與資料分區」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識計算分區能耗。設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 建立供電冷卻與設施的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是GPU Booster 與通用節點的工作流分工。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify compute-partition energy in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Leonardo Booster and data-centric partitions. Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of power, cooling and facilities, focusing on gpu booster and general-node workflow division. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交計算分區能耗的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for compute-partition energy.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-09-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：計算分區能耗","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: Compute-partition energy","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-09-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就計算分區能耗的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in compute-partition energy?","options":["低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。"],"optionsEn":["Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：證據驗證","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-leonardo-v11-09"],"objective":"針對計算分區能耗提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for compute-partition energy.","instruction":"沿用前一步「供電冷卻與設施」模型，檢查計算分區能耗的兩個假想案例。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous power, cooling and facilities model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving compute-partition energy. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交計算分區能耗的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for compute-partition energy.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-10-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：計算分區能耗","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: Compute-partition energy","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-10-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就計算分區能耗的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in compute-partition energy?","options":["覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"title":"排程隔離與復原：架構分析","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-leonardo-v11-10"],"objective":"針對跨分區排程提出可反駁的排程隔離與復原模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable scheduling, isolation and recovery model and evidence record for cross-partition scheduling.","instruction":"在「Leonardo Booster 與資料分區」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識跨分區排程。多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 建立排程隔離與復原的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是GPU Booster 與通用節點的工作流分工。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify cross-partition scheduling in the mentor diagram and primary sources for Leonardo Booster and data-centric partitions. Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of scheduling, isolation and recovery, focusing on gpu booster and general-node workflow division. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","observationEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table.","failure":"常見誤判：換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","check":"提交跨分區排程的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for cross-partition scheduling.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-11-k1","title":"排程隔離與復原","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery","text":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 本課架構對應：跨分區排程","textEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Course architecture correspondence: Cross-partition scheduling","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-11-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-11-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.025，使用 16 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=11.6364。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.025 and 16 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=11.6364. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就跨分區排程的「排程隔離與復原」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for scheduling, isolation and recovery in cross-partition scheduling?","options":["換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","explanationEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."}},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"title":"排程隔離與復原：證據驗證","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-leonardo-v11-11"],"objective":"針對跨分區排程提出可反駁的排程隔離與復原模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable scheduling, isolation and recovery model and evidence record for cross-partition scheduling.","instruction":"沿用前一步「排程隔離與復原」模型，檢查跨分區排程的兩個假想案例。在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous scheduling, isolation and recovery model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving cross-partition scheduling. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","observationEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table.","failure":"常見誤判：換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","check":"提交跨分區排程的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for cross-partition scheduling.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-12-k1","title":"排程隔離與復原","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery","text":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 本課架構對應：跨分區排程","textEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Course architecture correspondence: Cross-partition scheduling","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-12-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"]},{"id":"v11-leonardo-v11-12-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.025，使用 16 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=11.6364。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.025 and 16 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=11.6364. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo","v11x-perlmutter"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就跨分區排程的「排程隔離與復原」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for scheduling, isolation and recovery in cross-partition scheduling?","options":["換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","explanationEn":"Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table."}}]}],"summary":"以GPU Booster 與通用節點的工作流分工解析Leonardo Booster 與資料分區：六個原理與架構單元、十二項可保存的分析及驗證作業，附假想量化例、來源及衍生工程比較。","summaryEn":"Explore Leonardo Booster and data-centric partitions through gpu booster and general-node workflow division: six principle/architecture units and twelve saved analysis/validation tasks, with an assumed numerical example, primary sources and related engineering comparisons.","scope":"公開伺服器與超算架構的離線工作流、通信、儲存及能量模型；非機櫃接線、供電施工或實體維護SOP，也不表示學員取得廠商／研究中心設備存取。","scopeEn":"Offline workflow, fabric, storage and energy models of public servers/HPC. No rack-wiring, power-installation or physical-maintenance SOP and no vendor/research-center hardware access is implied.","workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.025，使用 16 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=11.6364。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.025 and 16 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=11.6364. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變模型邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are independently selected assumptions, not measured hardware, ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after boundary changes.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開架構及領域原理，不宣稱來源提供這組假想數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public architecture and principles, not these assumed measurements."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["Booster GPU與主機","InfiniBand層級","partition工作流","高效與容量存儲","計算分區能耗","跨分區排程"],"labelsEn":["Booster GPU and host","InfiniBand hierarchy","Partition workflows","Fast/capacity storage","Compute-partition energy","Cross-partition scheduling"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"vendorHints":[{"name":"CINECA","nameEn":"CINECA","url":"https://www.hpc.cineca.it/systems/hardware/leonardo/","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-leonardo"]},{"name":"NERSC","nameEn":"NERSC","url":"https://docs.nersc.gov/systems/perlmutter/architecture/","role":"官方工程或研究資料；不表示背書、授課或本平臺能訪問其設備。","roleEn":"Official engineering/research reference; no endorsement, teaching partnership or hardware access is implied.","sourceIds":["v11x-perlmutter"]}],"architectureNodes":[["計算節點","Compute nodes"],["本地記憶體","Local memory"],["叢集網路","Cluster fabric"],["儲存階層","Storage tiers"],["供電與冷卻","Power and cooling"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[0,2],[2,3],[4,0]],"architectureFamily":"server","educationEdition":11,"enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"v11-jupiter","title":"JUPITER 模組超算系統","titleEn":"JUPITER modular supercomputing system","category":"computing","subcategory":"servers-hpc","subcategoryTitle":"大型計算系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Large computing systems","learningTrack":"servers","learningSubdiscipline":"servers-hpc","learningTags":["servers","servers-hpc","jupiter"],"kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"curriculumVersion":11,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":420,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"stages":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-stage1","order":1,"title":"系統邊界與基本原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and principles","description":"在JUPITER 模組超算系統案例中比較GH200與CPU模塊與DragonFly+網絡，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate gh200 and cpu modules and dragonfly+ fabric within the JUPITER modular supercomputing system case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：架構分析","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"針對GH200與CPU模塊提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for gh200 and cpu modules.","instruction":"在「JUPITER 模組超算系統」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識GH200與CPU模塊。CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 建立節點與記憶體層級的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是Booster、Cluster 與多層儲存協作。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify gh200 and cpu modules in the mentor diagram and primary sources for JUPITER modular supercomputing system. CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of nodes and memory hierarchy, focusing on booster, cluster and tiered-storage cooperation. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交GH200與CPU模塊的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for gh200 and cpu modules.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-01-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：GH200與CPU模塊","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: GH200 and CPU modules","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-01-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-01-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.030，使用 24 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=14.2012。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.030 and 24 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=14.2012. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就GH200與CPU模塊的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in gh200 and cpu modules?","options":["CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。","統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.","Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"title":"節點與記憶體層級：證據驗證","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-jupiter-v11-01"],"objective":"針對GH200與CPU模塊提出可反駁的節點與記憶體層級模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable nodes and memory hierarchy model and evidence record for gh200 and cpu modules.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點與記憶體層級」模型，檢查GH200與CPU模塊的兩個假想案例。畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous nodes and memory hierarchy model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving gh200 and cpu modules. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","observationEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","failure":"常見誤判：統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","check":"提交GH200與CPU模塊的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for gh200 and cpu modules.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-02-k1","title":"節點與記憶體層級","titleEn":"Nodes and memory hierarchy","text":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 本課架構對應：GH200與CPU模塊","textEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Course architecture correspondence: GH200 and CPU modules","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-02-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-02-k3","title":"原創假想量化練習","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative exercise","text":"假設固定工作量有串行比例 0.030，使用 24 個理想同速工作者，Amdahl 上限 S=1/[f+(1−f)/N]=14.2012。通信、負載不均及I/O尚未計入，實效不得用此上限當實測。","textEn":"Assume serial fraction 0.030 and 24 ideal equal workers: Amdahl upper bound S=14.2012. Communication, imbalance and I/O are omitted; this bound is not measured performance.","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"就GH200與CPU模塊的「節點與記憶體層級」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for nodes and memory hierarchy in gh200 and cpu modules?","options":["統一地址空間等於所有內存同樣快。","畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Unified address space means all memory is equally fast.","Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"CPU、加速器及NUMA位置決定延遲與搬運；共享地址不意味着等距存取。 畫節點拓撲並比較本地與遠端假想訪存。","explanationEn":"CPUs, accelerators and NUMA placement determine latency/traffic; shared addresses do not imply uniform access. Draw node topology and compare local/remote assumed access."}},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：架構分析","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-jupiter-v11-02"],"objective":"針對DragonFly+網絡提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for dragonfly+ fabric.","instruction":"在「JUPITER 模組超算系統」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識DragonFly+網絡。高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 建立節點內與節點間網路的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是Booster、Cluster 與多層儲存協作。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify dragonfly+ fabric in the mentor diagram and primary sources for JUPITER modular supercomputing system. Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of intranode and internode networks, focusing on booster, cluster and tiered-storage cooperation. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交DragonFly+網絡的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for dragonfly+ fabric.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-03-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：DragonFly+網絡","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: DragonFly+ fabric","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-03-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就DragonFly+網絡的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in dragonfly+ fabric?","options":["節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。"],"optionsEn":["Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"title":"節點內與節點間網路：證據驗證","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-jupiter-v11-03"],"objective":"針對DragonFly+網絡提出可反駁的節點內與節點間網路模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable intranode and internode networks model and evidence record for dragonfly+ fabric.","instruction":"沿用前一步「節點內與節點間網路」模型，檢查DragonFly+網絡的兩個假想案例。按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous intranode and internode networks model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving dragonfly+ fabric. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","observationEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","failure":"常見誤判：節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","check":"提交DragonFly+網絡的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for dragonfly+ fabric.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-04-k1","title":"節點內與節點間網路","titleEn":"Intranode and internode networks","text":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 本課架構對應：DragonFly+網絡","textEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Course architecture correspondence: DragonFly+ fabric","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-04-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就DragonFly+網絡的「節點內與節點間網路」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for intranode and internode networks in dragonfly+ fabric?","options":["按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","節點內GPU互連規格等於跨機櫃網絡規格。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth.","Intranode GPU rates equal interrack fabric rates.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高速內連與外部網絡有不同路由、端點與割頻寬；性能需分層。 按perlink、pernode及system標註雙向頻寬。","explanationEn":"Internal/external fabrics differ in routes, endpoints and bisection; evaluate by layer. Label bidirectional per-link, per-node and system bandwidth."}}]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-stage2","order":2,"title":"功能架構與量化模型","titleEn":"Functional architecture and quantitative models","description":"在JUPITER 模組超算系統案例中比較模塊化工作分割與ExaFLASH/STORE/TAPE，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate modular workload partition and exaflash/store/tape within the JUPITER modular supercomputing system case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：架構分析","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-jupiter-v11-04"],"objective":"針對模塊化工作分割提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for modular workload partition.","instruction":"在「JUPITER 模組超算系統」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識模塊化工作分割。串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 建立工作分割與平行效率的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是Booster、Cluster 與多層儲存協作。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify modular workload partition in the mentor diagram and primary sources for JUPITER modular supercomputing system. Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of work partition and parallel efficiency, focusing on booster, cluster and tiered-storage cooperation. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交模塊化工作分割的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for modular workload partition.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-05-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：模塊化工作分割","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: Modular workload partition","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-05-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就模塊化工作分割的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in modular workload partition?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"title":"工作分割與平行效率：證據驗證","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-jupiter-v11-05"],"objective":"針對模塊化工作分割提出可反駁的工作分割與平行效率模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable work partition and parallel efficiency model and evidence record for modular workload partition.","instruction":"沿用前一步「工作分割與平行效率」模型，檢查模塊化工作分割的兩個假想案例。對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous work partition and parallel efficiency model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving modular workload partition. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","observationEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work.","failure":"常見誤判：峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","check":"提交模塊化工作分割的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for modular workload partition.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-06-k1","title":"工作分割與平行效率","titleEn":"Work partition and parallel efficiency","text":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 本課架構對應：模塊化工作分割","textEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Course architecture correspondence: Modular workload partition","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-06-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就模塊化工作分割的「工作分割與平行效率」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for work partition and parallel efficiency in modular workload partition?","options":["峯值算力翻倍保證每個應用時間減半。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling peak compute halves every application runtime.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."],"answer":2,"explanation":"串行部分、負載不均與通信限制擴充；峯值FLOPS不是應用耗時。 對固定工作量重算Amdahl上限和通信餘量。","explanationEn":"Serial work, imbalance and communication limit scaling; peak FLOPS are not application time. Recalculate Amdahl bounds/communication margins for fixed work."}},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：架構分析","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-jupiter-v11-06"],"objective":"針對ExaFLASH/STORE/TAPE提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for exaflash/store/tape.","instruction":"在「JUPITER 模組超算系統」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識ExaFLASH/STORE/TAPE。暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 建立儲存階層與檢查點的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是Booster、Cluster 與多層儲存協作。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify exaflash/store/tape in the mentor diagram and primary sources for JUPITER modular supercomputing system. Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of storage tiers and checkpoints, focusing on booster, cluster and tiered-storage cooperation. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交ExaFLASH/STORE/TAPE的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for exaflash/store/tape.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-07-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：ExaFLASH/STORE/TAPE","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: ExaFLASH/STORE/TAPE","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-07-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就ExaFLASH/STORE/TAPE的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in exaflash/store/tape?","options":["暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。","容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.","Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"title":"儲存階層與檢查點：證據驗證","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-jupiter-v11-07"],"objective":"針對ExaFLASH/STORE/TAPE提出可反駁的儲存階層與檢查點模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable storage tiers and checkpoints model and evidence record for exaflash/store/tape.","instruction":"沿用前一步「儲存階層與檢查點」模型，檢查ExaFLASH/STORE/TAPE的兩個假想案例。比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous storage tiers and checkpoints model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving exaflash/store/tape. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","observationEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","failure":"常見誤判：容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","check":"提交ExaFLASH/STORE/TAPE的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for exaflash/store/tape.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-08-k1","title":"儲存階層與檢查點","titleEn":"Storage tiers and checkpoints","text":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 本課架構對應：ExaFLASH/STORE/TAPE","textEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Course architecture correspondence: ExaFLASH/STORE/TAPE","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-08-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就ExaFLASH/STORE/TAPE的「儲存階層與檢查點」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for storage tiers and checkpoints in exaflash/store/tape?","options":["容量大表示小檔隨機訪問一定快。","比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Large capacity guarantees fast random small-file access.","Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暫存、容量與歸檔層服務不同I/O；檢查點需考慮寫入和恢復成本。 比較順序、隨機及metadata的假想時間預算。","explanationEn":"Scratch, capacity and archive serve different I/O; checkpoints need write/recovery costs. Compare assumed sequential, random and metadata time budgets."}}]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-stage3","order":3,"title":"獨立驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Independent validation and engineering handoff","description":"在JUPITER 模組超算系統案例中比較溫水冷卻邊界與模塊排程與故障恢復，各完成分析及驗證。","descriptionEn":"Analyze and validate warm-water cooling boundary and module scheduling/recovery within the JUPITER modular supercomputing system case.","steps":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：架構分析","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-jupiter-v11-08"],"objective":"針對溫水冷卻邊界提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for warm-water cooling boundary.","instruction":"在「JUPITER 模組超算系統」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識溫水冷卻邊界。設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 建立供電冷卻與設施的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是Booster、Cluster 與多層儲存協作。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify warm-water cooling boundary in the mentor diagram and primary sources for JUPITER modular supercomputing system. Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of power, cooling and facilities, focusing on booster, cluster and tiered-storage cooperation. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交溫水冷卻邊界的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for warm-water cooling boundary.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-09-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：溫水冷卻邊界","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: Warm-water cooling boundary","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-09-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就溫水冷卻邊界的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in warm-water cooling boundary?","options":["低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。","設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。"],"optionsEn":["Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors.","Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"title":"供電冷卻與設施：證據驗證","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities: evidence validation","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-jupiter-v11-09"],"objective":"針對溫水冷卻邊界提出可反駁的供電冷卻與設施模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable power, cooling and facilities model and evidence record for warm-water cooling boundary.","instruction":"沿用前一步「供電冷卻與設施」模型，檢查溫水冷卻邊界的兩個假想案例。覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 先訂可接受誤差，再比較預測與獨立計算；區分設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。與另一個可能造成相同輸出的機制。保存輸入、殘差、不確定度及採信／保留理由。缺少公開資料就標示尚未驗證，不補造產品數字。","instructionEn":"Use the previous power, cooling and facilities model to inspect two hypothetical cases involving warm-water cooling boundary. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Set acceptable error before comparing predictions with an independent calculation. Distinguish \"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result.\" from an alternative cause with similar output. Save inputs, residuals, uncertainty and accept/hold reasoning. Mark absent public evidence as unverified rather than inventing product values.","observation":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","observationEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","failure":"常見誤判：低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","check":"提交溫水冷卻邊界的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for warm-water cooling boundary.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-10-k1","title":"供電冷卻與設施","titleEn":"Power, cooling and facilities","text":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 本課架構對應：溫水冷卻邊界","textEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Course architecture correspondence: Warm-water cooling boundary","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-10-k2","title":"獨立驗證與失效邊界","titleEn":"Independent validation and breakdown boundary","text":"覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。 應逐項保留基準與不確定度；低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。 是本單元要排除的誤解。","textEn":"Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries. Retain each reference and uncertainty; reject the misconception: Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"]}],"quiz":{"question":"就溫水冷卻邊界的「供電冷卻與設施」，哪個推論或驗證成立？","questionEn":"Which inference or check is justified for power, cooling and facilities in warm-water cooling boundary?","options":["覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","低PUE保證相同任務計算能耗最低。","兩個案例的平均相同，就足以排除空間、時間及模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries.","Low PUE guarantees minimum compute energy for a task.","Equal case averages rule out spatial, temporal and model errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"設施功率包含IT與輔助；PUE不能單獨判定計算結果每單位能耗。 覈對IT、總設施及作業時間的能量邊界。","explanationEn":"Facility power includes IT/auxiliary loads; PUE alone does not specify energy per result. Check IT, facility and job-time energy boundaries."}},{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"title":"排程隔離與復原：架構分析","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery: architecture analysis","estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11x-jupiter","v11x-alps"],"prerequisiteIds":["v11-jupiter-v11-10"],"objective":"針對模塊排程與故障恢復提出可反駁的排程隔離與復原模型與驗證紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Produce a falsifiable scheduling, isolation and recovery model and evidence record for module scheduling/recovery.","instruction":"在「JUPITER 模組超算系統」的師傅示意與公開來源中，先辨識模塊排程與故障恢復。多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢復。 建立排程隔離與復原的輸入、狀態、輸出及邊界圖；本課重點是Booster、Cluster 與多層儲存協作。用本課假想算例建立基準，再只改一個相關假設，預測哪個輸出先變。在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。 記錄單位、未公開參數及模型失效條件。","instructionEn":"Identify module scheduling/recovery in the mentor diagram and primary sources for JUPITER modular supercomputing system. Multi-tenant jobs need limits/recoverable state; hardware availability is not application recovery. Draw the inputs, states, outputs and boundaries of scheduling, isolation and recovery, focusing on booster, cluster and tiered-storage cooperation. Establish a baseline with the hypothetical worked example, change one relevant assumption and predict the first affected output. Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table. Record units, undisclosed parameters and model breakdown conditions.","observation":"在離線事件表追蹤節點失效、重排與結果一致性。","observationEn":"Trace failures, rescheduling and result consistency in an offline event table.","failure":"常見誤判：換一臺節點就無需校驗恢復後的狀態。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Replacing a node requires no recovered-state validation.","check":"提交模塊排程與故障恢復的系統邊界圖、兩案例計算、單位／不確定度表及一項能區分競爭機制的證據。","checkEn":"Submit a boundary diagram, two-case calculation, units/uncertainty table and discriminating evidence for module scheduling/recovery.","knowledge":[{"id":"v11-jupiter-v11-11-k1","title":"排程隔離與復原","titleEn":"Scheduling, isolation and recovery","text":"多租戶作業需資源限制與可恢復狀態；硬體可用不等於應用已恢�